window.EF_CRUX_DOC_PAGES=["ARRIVAL OF EUROPEAN COMPANIES IN INDIA — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 1 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Establishment vs Factory-in-India — SABSE BADA TRAP\n●Europe mein establish: Portuguese(1498) → English(1600) → Dutch(1602) → Danish(1616) → French(1664) →\nSwedish(1731)\n●India mein pehli factory: Portuguese(1503) → Dutch(1605) → English(1613) → Danish(1620) → French(1668)\n TRICK — \"Dutch baad mein bane, PEHLE factory lagayi\" trick\n💡\nDutch(VOC) English se 2 saal BAAD company bani(1602 vs 1600 English), lekin India mein factory 8 saal PEHLE\nlagayi(1605 vs 1613 English) — \"der se aaye, jaldi laga li dukaan\" — is ulta-pattern ko ek line mein yaad rakho, ye\npoore chapter ka SABSE common trap hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDutch VOC(1602) English EIC(1600) ke BAAD bani Europe mein, LEKIN India mein Dutch factory(1605) English\nfactory(1613) se PEHLE lagi — establishment-date aur factory-date do alag timelines hain.\n2. Portuguese — State Power, Company NAHI\n●Portuguese = State power(Portugal desh khud involve) — baaki sab(EIC,VOC,French,Danish) = formal TRADING\nCOMPANIES\n●\"1498\" = sirf arrival date, koi company-formation date nahi\n TRICK — \"Akela State\" trick\n💡\n5 mein se sirf Portuguese State hai, baaki 4 Companies hain — \"Portuguese = Pora desh(poora country) khud aaya\"\n— is akele-alag-hone wale fact ko yaad rakho, exam isi angle se pakadta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPortuguese ek STATE POWER tha, koi trading company nahi. 1498 = sirf arrival date, company-formation date NAHI\n(kyunki company thi hi nahi).\n3. Houtman — India NAHI, Indonesia Gaya\n●Houtman(1596) = Dutch traveler → Indonesia(Sumatra) gaya, India NAHI\n TRICK — \"Houtman = Indonesia\" trick\n💡\nHoutman — \"Hout\" jaisa sound \"Out(bahar/door)\" se milta hai — \"Out-of-India, Indonesia gaya\" — ye ek word-play\nse hi yaad rah jaata hai ki Houtman India nahi gaya tha.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHoutman(1596) Indonesia(Sumatra) gaya tha, India NAHI — chapter ka sabse zyada confuse karne wala naam.\n4. \"1st Factory\" — Context Pe Depend Karta Hai\n●Overall 1st European factory in India = Portuguese, Cochin(1503)\n●English 1st TEMPORARY factory = Masulipatnam(1611, South India)\n●English 1st PERMANENT factory = Surat(1613, Director Thomas Aldworth)\n TRICK — \"3 alag \\\"1st factory\\\" answers\" trick\n💡","Sawaal ka wording padho: \"India ki PEHLI factory\" → Cochin(Portuguese,1503). \"English ki pehli TEMPORARY\"\n→ Masulipatnam(1611). \"English ki pehli PERMANENT\" → Surat(1613). Teeno alag\nqualifiers(overall/temporary/permanent) — teen alag jawab.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"1st factory in India\" ka jawab wording pe depend karta hai: Overall=Cochin(Portuguese,1503). English\ntemporary=Masulipatnam(1611). English permanent=Surat(1613,Aldworth).\n5. Vasco da Gama — 3 Trips\n●1st(May 1498): Calicut → Zamorin(local raja) se mile\n●2nd(1502): Re-arrival\n●3rd(1524): Cochin mein guzar gaye(death)\n TRICK — \"Aaya-Aaya-Mar gaya\" trick\n💡\n3 trips ka pattern: 1st=arrival(khushi), 2nd=re-arrival(routine), 3rd=death(end) — \"pehli baar naya desh dekha,\ndoosri baar dobara aaya, teesri baar wahin mar gaya\" — ek life-story jaisi teen-step chain.\n6. Portuguese 3 Governors — Alag-Alag Kaam\n●Almeida(1505-09) = 1st Governor · Blue Water Policy(sea control) · Cartaz System(sea-pass)\n●Albuquerque(1509-15) = REAL founder of Portuguese power · Goa capture(1510) · Sati discourage\n●Nino da Cunha(1529-38) = Bassein(1534)+Diu(1535) capture · HQ Cochin→Goa shift\n TRICK — \"Almeida=Policy, Albuquerque=Founder, Cunha=HQ-shift\" trick\n💡\nAlmeida = \"Alag/pehla policy-maker\"(Blue Water+Cartaz). Albuquerque = \"Alpha/asli founder\"(dono naam \"Al\" se\nshuru hote hain isliye confuse hota hai — par Albuquerque hi REAL founder hai, Goa bhi usi ne liya). Cunha = \"naya\nHQ laya\"(Goa) — 3 alag roles, 3 alag governors.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBlue Water Policy = Almeida ki (Albuquerque ki NAHI). Albuquerque = Portuguese power ke REAL founder,\nGoa(1510) usne capture kiya.\n7. French — 3 Carnatic Wars, Teeno Mein Haare\n●3 Carnatic Wars(1746-1763) vs British → French TEENO mein haare\n●Pondicherry(1674) = Sher Khan Lodi se mila → French ka main base\n●Surat(1668) = French ki 1st factory, founder Francis Caron\n TRICK — \"3-0 loss\" trick\n💡\nFrench ka Carnatic Wars record = 0 jeet, 3 haar — \"French = Fail teeno baar\" — F se F, French aur Fail dono match\nkarte hain, is simple hook se count(3) aur result(haar) dono yaad reh jaate hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nFrench vs British = 3 Carnatic Wars(1746-1763) — French TEENO mein haare. Count kabhi 2 ya 4 mat karna, exact 3\nhai.\n8. Danish Exit vs Dutch Exit — Bilkul Alag Style\n●Dutch → Battle of Bedara/Biderra(1759) mein British se HAARE → exit\n●Danish → Battle mein NAHI haare → 1845 mein factories British ko BECH DI(peacefully)","TRICK — \"Haara vs Becha\" trick\n💡\nDutch = Lada aur Haara(Bedara, 1759). Danish = Bina lade Becha(1845, peaceful sale) — \"Dutch Defeated(war),\nDanish Deal(sale)\" — dono \"D\" se shuru hote hain isliye confuse hota hai, par ek WAR se gaya, doosra SALE se gaya.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDutch = Battle of Bedara(1759) mein HAARE(defeat se exit). Danish = 1845 mein factories British ko BECH DI (battle\nmein nahi haare) — dono ka exit-style bilkul alag hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Establish order: Portuguese(1498)-English(1600)-Dutch(1602)-Danish(1616)-French(1664)-Swedish(1731) → Factory\norder: Portuguese(1503,Cochin)-Dutch(1605)-English(1613,Surat)-Danish(1620)-French(1668) → Dutch:baad-mein-\nbana,pehle-factory → Portuguese=State not Company → Houtman=Indonesia not India → VascoDaGama:\nCalicut(1498)-rearrival(1502)-death(1524,Cochin) → Governors: Almeida(BlueWater,Cartaz)-Albuquerque(real\nfounder,Goa1510)-Cunha(HQ shift Goa) → French: 3 Carnatic Wars,3 haar,Pondicherry(1674) →\nDutch=haare(Bedara1759) vs Danish=becha(1845)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Dutch(1602) English(1600) ke baad bane, par Dutch factory(1605) English factory(1613) se pehle lagi.\n2) Houtman(1596) Indonesia gaya tha, India NAHI.\n3) Dutch=battle mein haare(Bedara,1759). Danish=battle mein nahi haare, factories BECH di(1845).\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.1 European Companies in India","BRITISH EXPANSION IN INDIAN TERRITORIES — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 2 (Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 3 Presidencies — 3 Alag Tareeke Se Mili\n●Madras(1639) = LEASE(Francis Day, King of Chandragiri se) → Fort St. George\n●Bombay(1661) = DOWRY(Charles II ki shaadi, Catherine of Braganza se) — Conquest NAHI!\n●Calcutta(1698) = ZAMINDARI RIGHTS KHAREEDI(3 gaon: Sutanuti,Kalikata,Govindpur) → Fort William\n TRICK — \"Lease-Dowry-Kharidi\" trick\n💡\n3 alag \"kaise mila\" answers: Madras=LEASE(kiraya), Bombay=DOWRY(shaadi ka tohfa), Calcutta=BUY(zameen\nkhareedi) — teeno bilkul alag tareeke, ek bhi \"jung/conquest\" se NAHI mila. \"Bombay to shaadi mein mila, ladai\nmein nahi\" — ye SABSE common trap hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBombay CONQUEST mein nahi, DOWRY mein mila (1661, Charles II ki shaadi Catherine of Braganza se) — ye\nchapter ka sabse famous trap hai.\n2. Plassey(1757) vs Buxar(1764) — Commander Trap\n●Plassey(23 June 1757) = Robert Clive vs Siraj-ud-Daulah → Mir Jafar ne betray kiya\n●Buxar(22 Oct 1764) = Hector Munro vs 3-alliance(Mir Qasim+Shuja-ud-Daulah+Shah Alam II)\n TRICK — \"Clive=Plassey, Munro=Buxar\" trick\n💡\n7 saal ka gap(1757→1764), aur commander bhi badal gaya: Clive PEHLE(Plassey), Munro BAAD mein(Buxar) —\n\"Clive Chota war jeeta pehle(1 opponent-Siraj), Munro Mushkil war jeeta baad mein(3 opponents combined)\" — jitna\nbada alliance utna naya commander.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPlassey(1757)=Robert Clive. Buxar(1764)=Hector Munro — Robert Clive ko Buxar mein mat dena, ye sabse common\nexam trap hai.\n3. Black Hole Tragedy(1756) — Holwell Ka Version Use Karo\n●Holwell claim(exam mein yehi use hota): 146 imprisoned, 23 survive\n●Modern historians estimate ALAG hai(~64 imprisoned,~43 died) — par BPSC/BSSC mein Holwell ke figures hi\ncorrect maane jaate hain\n TRICK — \"Exam=Holwell, Reality=Alag\" trick\n💡\nYaad rakho: \"Holwell ka Hi number chalega exam mein\" — 146/23 — chahe historians disagree karte hon, EXAM\nCONTEXT mein hamesha Holwell ka version sahi jawab hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBlack Hole Tragedy: Holwell ka version(146 imprisoned, 23 survive) exam mein use hota hai — modern\nestimate(~64/~43) NAHI, chahe wo zyada accurate ho.\n4. Mir Jafar — 2 BAAR Nawab\n●Mir Jafar(1757-1760) → Mir Qasim(1760-1763) → Mir Jafar WAPAS(1763-1765)","TRICK — \"Jafar-Qasim-Jafar\" sandwich trick\n💡\nEk \"sandwich\" pattern: Jafar(bread)-Qasim(filling)-Jafar(bread) — Mir Qasim BEECH mein aaya, Jafar dono\ntaraf(shuru+ant) — \"J-Q-J\" bolke yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMir Jafar DO BAAR Nawab tha: 1757-60 aur phir 1763-65. Beech mein Mir Qasim(1760-63) tha — sequence: Jafar-\nQasim-Jafar.\n5. 3 Carnatic Wars — Treaty Match\n●1st(1746-48) → Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle — status quo\n●2nd(1749-54) → Treaty of Pondicherry(1755) — Dupleix recall\n●3rd(1756-63) → Treaty of Paris(1763) — French power khatam\n●Wandiwash(1760, 3rd war ki battle): Eyre Coote(British,jeeta) vs Count de Lally(French,haara)\n TRICK — \"APP\" treaty trick\n💡\nAix-la-Chapelle(1st) → Pondicherry(2nd) → Paris(3rd) = \"APP\" — bas is short-code se teeno treaty yaad rakho: A\npehle, phir do P's.\nWandiwash = Eyre Coote(jeete) vs Lally(haare) — dono naam exam mein direct poochhe jaate hain, cross mat karo\nwinner-loser.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1st Carnatic War=Aix-la-Chapelle treaty. 2nd=Pondicherry treaty(Dupleix recall). 3rd=Paris treaty(French power\nkhatam). Wandiwash(1760)=Eyre Coote(British) ne Count de Lally(French) ko haraya.\n6. 4 Anglo-Mysore Wars — Governor-General Match\n●1st(1767-69) → Koi GG nahi mentioned → Treaty of Madras(1769)\n●2nd(1780-84) → Warren Hastings → Treaty of Mangalore(1784)\n●3rd(1790-92) → Cornwallis → Treaty of Seringapatam(1792)\n●4th(1799) → Wellesley → Tipu maare gaye\n TRICK — \"None-Hastings-Cornwallis-Wellesley\" trick\n💡\n4 wars, pehli mein koi GG naam nahi(sabse purani, before-GG-system-established jaisa), phir 3 alag GGs: Warren\nHastings(2nd)-Cornwallis(3rd)-Wellesley(4th) — jaise GG-system dheere-dheere strong hui, waise hi har war mein\nnaya bada naam aaya.\n4th war mein Tipu khud maare gaye — is finality se yaad rakho ki 4th war hi Mysore ka poora ant hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAnglo-Mysore Wars GG: 1st=koi nahi. 2nd=Warren Hastings(Mangalore,1784). 3rd=Cornwallis(Seringapatam,1792).\n4th=Wellesley(Tipu death,1799).\n7. 1st Anglo-Afghan War(1839-42) — DISASTER\n●Lord Auckland ke time → British HAARE, Kabul se RETREAT karna pada — chapter ki EKLAUTI badi British\nhaar\n●Sindh(1843) annex hua — ye ALAG event hai, same time period mein\n TRICK — \"Sirf Afghan mein British haare\" trick\n💡\nPoore chapter mein British ne har jagah jeeta — Mysore,Punjab,Burma sab jagah — SIRF Afghanistan(1st war) mein\nDISASTROUS haar hui. Ye chapter ka SABSE UNIQUE fact hai(only-loss), isse alag se yaad rakho.\nSindh annexation(1843) Afghan war se ALAG event hai — same time period mein hua isliye confuse hota hai, par\ndono independent facts hain.","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1st Anglo-Afghan War(1839-42, Lord Auckland) British ke liye DISASTROUS thi — Kabul se retreat. Sindh(1843)\nannexation ALAG event hai, same period mein.\n8. Punjab — Treaty of Amritsar + 2 Anglo-Sikh Wars\n●Treaty of Amritsar(1809): Ranjit Singh + Lord Metcalfe → Sutlej boundary\n●1st Anglo-Sikh War(1845-46): Sikhs haare → Treaty of Lahore(9 March 1846)\n●2nd(1848-49): Ramnagar→Chillianwala→Gujrat → March 1849 poora Punjab annex\n TRICK — Cross-chapter callback\n💡\nYe detail Rise of the Sikhs chapter mein bhi tha — is chapter mein sirf timeline recall karo: 1809(treaty)→1845-46(1st\nwar)→1848-49(2nd war,annex).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"3 Presidencies: Madras-Lease,Bombay-Dowry,Calcutta-Buy → Plassey(1757,Clive) vs Buxar(1764,Munro) →\nBlackHole=Holwell(146/23) → Nawabs: Jafar-Qasim-Jafar → Carnatic: APP treaties(AixLaChapelle-Pondicherry-\nParis),Wandiwash(Coote beat Lally) → Mysore GGs: None-WarrenHastings-Cornwallis-Wellesley →\nAfghanWar1(1839-42)=DISASTER(sirf British haar) → Punjab: Amritsar1809-1stAnglo-Sikh1845-46-2ndAnglo-\nSikh1848-49(annex)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGHEST WEIGHTAGE chapter hai.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Bombay=DOWRY mila(1661), conquest se NAHI.\n2) Plassey(1757)=Clive. Buxar(1764)=Hector Munro — swap mat karo.\n3) Anglo-Mysore Wars GG: 1st=none, 2nd=Warren Hastings, 3rd=Cornwallis, 4th=Wellesley.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.2 British Expansion in Indian Territories","THE REVOLT OF 1857 — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 3 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Plassey(1757) + 100 Saal = Revolt(1857)\n●1757 Plassey(British power ki shuruaat) → THEEK 100 saal baad → 1857 Revolt(sabse badi bagawat)\n●GG: Lord Canning(baad mein pehla Viceroy) · British PM: Lord Palmerston\n TRICK — \"100-saal-symmetry\" trick\n💡\n7-5-7 se 8-5-7 — dono saal mein \"57\" common hai(1757, 1857)! Jis saal British power SHURU hui, exactly usi ke 100-\nsaal-baad unhe sabse badi CHALLENGE mili — is symmetry se hi dono dates lock ho jaati hain.\n2. Causes — 4 Categories\n●Political: Doctrine of Lapse(Dalhousie) — Satara(1848),Sambalpur(1849),Jhansi(1853) · Subsidiary\nAlliance(Wellesley)\n●Economic: Permanent Settlement, Ryotwari, Mahalwari — sab kisaan-nuksaan wale\n●Social: Missionaries, racial discrimination, social-reform-backlash(Sati/child-marriage ban)\n●Immediate/Trigger: Enfield Rifle — cartridge mein Cow fat(Hindu) + Pig fat(Muslim) rumour\n TRICK — \"Dalhousie=Lapse, Wellesley=Alliance\" trick\n💡\nDalhousie=Lapse(D-L), Wellesley=Alliance(dono \"W\" jaisa lagta hai but alag) — Doctrine of Lapse aur Subsidiary\nAlliance dono POLITICAL causes hain par ALAG GG ne diye. Enfield Rifle sirf trigger/spark tha, background cause\nNAHI — baaki sab pehle se ubal rahe the.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDoctrine of Lapse = Dalhousie. Subsidiary Alliance = Wellesley. Enfield Rifle = sirf IMMEDIATE/trigger cause, baaki\n3 categories(political/economic/social) background causes hain.\n3. Revolt Ki Shuruaat — 3 Alag Dates\n●29 March 1857(Barrackpore) → Mangal Pandey → 34th Native Infantry → \"Maro Firangi Ko\" → Officers:\nLt.Baugh + Sgt-Major Hewson(\"Major Hudson\" GALAT hai)\n●10 May 1857(Meerut) → ASLI/OFFICIAL start → \"Chalo Delhi\" naara\n●11 May 1857(Delhi) → Bahadur Shah Zafar Emperor ghoshit, real command = General Bakht Khan\n TRICK — \"29-10-11\" three-date trick\n💡\nMangal Pandey(29 Mar) = individual spark(spontaneous, ek akela sipahi). Meerut(10 May) = official/organized\nstart. Delhi(11 May) = symbolic capital capture(agle hi din) — teen alag stages: individual-protest → organized-\nrevolt → symbolic-capital, EK EK din/mahine ka gap.\nBaugh+Hewson — \"Major Hudson\" naam GALAT hai, is verified-correction ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMangal Pandey incident(29 Mar 1857,Barrackpore) ≠ Official revolt start(10 May 1857,Meerut) ≠ Delhi capture(11 May\n1857) — teeno alag dates. Officers ke sahi naam: Lt.Baugh+Sgt-Major HEWSON(NOT 'Major Hudson').\n4. Bahadur Shah Zafar — Symbolic, NOT Real Command\n●Zafar = symbolic/nominal Emperor — declared \"Shahenshah-e-Hindustan\"\n●General Bakht Khan = REAL military command\n TRICK — \"Naam ka raja, kaam ka General\" trick\n💡","Same pattern jo baar-baar dikha hai(Sadasiva Raya/Rama Raya, Chandragupta/real-founder): Zafar = title-holder,\nBakht Khan = actual power — \"naam-mein Emperor, kaam-mein General\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBahadur Shah Zafar sirf SYMBOLIC leader tha. Real military command = General Bakht Khan — ye exam mein direct\npoocha jaata hai.\n5. Centre-Wise Leaders — Direct Match\n●Delhi: Zafar+Bakht Khan vs Nicholson · Lucknow: Begum Hazrat Mahal(Nepal bhaagi) vs Colin Campbell\n●Kanpur: Nana Saheb+Tantia Tope vs Havelock · Jhansi: Rani Laxmibai vs Hugh Rose\n●Arrah/Bihar: Kunwar Singh(~80 saal, SABSE BUDHE) vs William Taylor · Gwalior: Tantia Tope — REVOLT\nYAHIN KHATAM(20 June 1858)\n TRICK — \"Hugh Rose Quote\" + \"Kunwar Singh Age\" trick\n💡\nHugh Rose(British commander) ne Laxmibai ke baare mein kaha: \"The only man among rebels\" — ye QUOTE\nBRITISH ki taraf se hai, Laxmibai khud ne nahi kaha — is direction ko yaad rakho.\nKunwar Singh = ~80 saal, sabse budhe par sabse bahadur rebel — age-fact khud unique hai isliye alag se yaad reh jaata\nhai.\nGwalior = revolt ka AAKHRI centre(20 June 1858) — Tantia Tope wahi tak lade, revolt ka poora ant yahin hua.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"The only man among rebels\" = Hugh Rose(British commander) ka quote Rani Laxmibai ke baare mein — khud\nLaxmibai ka quote NAHI. Kunwar Singh(~80 saal) = sabse budhe rebel leader.\n6. Failure — 4 Reasons\n●South India + Punjab BILKUL SHAANT rahe(limited geographic spread)\n●Limited social base(educated class,zamindars ne saath nahi diya)\n●Central leadership ki kami(Zafar sirf symbolic)\n●British ke better resources(telegraph+railways)\n TRICK — \"South+Punjab Shaant\" trick\n💡\nSouth India aur Punjab poori tarah SHAANT rahe — is geographic-limitation ko sabse pehle yaad rakho, kyunki\nexam isko highlight karta hai. Baaki 3 reasons(social-base, leadership, resources) sab \"kami/weakness\" hain, par\ngeography wala fact SABSE specific hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSouth India aur Punjab revolt ke time BILKUL SHAANT rahe — ye ek key geographic-limitation fact hai jo failure ka\nbada reason tha.\n7. Historians Ki Opinion — Match Karo\n●V.D. Savarkar(\"The Indian War of Independence,1857\") = PEHLE isse \"War of Independence\" kehne wale\n●R.C. Majumdar = \"Neither first, nor national, nor war of independence\" — Savarkar ke bilkul ULTA\n●Disraeli(British MP!) = \"National Revolt\" — khud British hote hue bhi positive view\n●S.N. Sen = Official Government Historian · Ashok Mehta = \"Great Rebellion\" · T.R. Holmes = \"Civilisation vs\nBarbarism\"\n TRICK — \"Savarkar-First, Majumdar-Opposite, Disraeli-Surprising\" trick\n💡\nSavarkar = PEHLA kehne wala(War of Independence). Majumdar = SEEDHA VIRODH(Savarkar ka opposite).\nDisraeli = SURPRISING(British hote hue bhi \"National Revolt\" kaha) — 3 sabse important historians, 3 alag angle:","pehla, opposite, surprising.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSavarkar = SABSE PEHLE \"War of Independence\" kaha. Majumdar = \"Neither first, nor national, nor war of\nindependence\" (Savarkar ke opposite). Disraeli = British MP hote hue bhi \"National Revolt\" kaha.\n8. After 1857 — Government of India Act, 1858\n●EIC ka rule khatam(1600 se 1858 tak, 258 saal) · Crown(Queen Victoria) supreme authority ban gayi\n●Governor-General → Viceroy designation badla · Lord Canning = FIRST Viceroy\n TRICK — \"258-saal-ka-ant\" trick\n💡\n1600(EIC bani) → 1858(EIC khatam) = poore 258 saal — is bade number se hi yaad rakho ki kitna bada shift tha\n\"Company Rule → Crown Rule\". Canning = same-vyakti jo LAST Governor-General bhi tha aur FIRST Viceroy bhi\n— designation badla, aadmi wahi raha.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Plassey(1757)+100=Revolt(1857) → Causes: Dalhousie-Lapse,Wellesley-Alliance,Enfield-trigger →\n29Mar(MangalPandey,Barrackpore)→10May(Meerut,official)→11May(Delhi,Zafar) →\nZafar=symbolic,BakhtKhan=real command → Centres:\nDelhi,Lucknow(HazratMahal),Kanpur(NanaSaheb+TantiaTope),Jhansi(Laxmibai-HughRose\nquote),Arrah(KunwarSingh~80yrs),Gwalior(revolt ends 20June1858) → Failure: South+Punjab shaant,weak\nleadership,British resources → Historians: Savarkar(first)-Majumdar(opposite)-Disraeli(surprising) → GoI Act1858:\nEIC-258yrs-khatam, Canning=lastGG+1stViceroy\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Mangal Pandey(29 Mar,Barrackpore) ≠ Official start(10 May,Meerut) ≠ Delhi capture(11 May) — teen alag dates.\n2) Bahadur Shah Zafar=symbolic. General Bakht Khan=real military command.\n3) \"The only man among rebels\" = Hugh Rose(British) ka quote Laxmibai ke baare mein, khud unka nahi.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.3 The Revolt of 1857","PEASANT MOVEMENTS & TRIBAL REVOLTS — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 4 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Champaran(1917) vs Kheda(1918) — Dono Gandhi Ke, Alag Hain\n●Champaran(1917) = 1st Gandhian Satyagraha · Bihar · Indigo farmers · Tinkathia System ke against\n●Kheda(1918) = Gandhi+Patel · Gujarat · Famine ke time bhi tax badha diya\n TRICK — \"Cham-1st, Kheda-2nd\" trick\n💡\nChamparan = Gandhi ka PEHLA satyagraha(1917,indigo/Bihar) — is \"FIRST\" ka tag hamesha Champaran ke saath\nhi rahega. Kheda(1918) ek saal baad, alag state(Gujarat), alag issue(tax-during-famine) — \"pehla=Champaran,\ndusra=Kheda\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChamparan(1917,Bihar,indigo/Tinkathia) = 1st Gandhian Satyagraha. Kheda(1918,Gujarat,famine-tax) = alag movement\n— dono Gandhi ke hain par mix mat karo.\n2. Bardoli(1928) — \"Sardar\" Title\n●Vallabhbhai Patel ko \"Sardar\" title mila Bardoli(Gujarat) ki jeet ke baad — Gandhi ne NAHI, leader Patel the\n TRICK — \"Bardoli=Sardar\" hook\n💡\nBardoli-Sardar — dono \"ar\" sound se rhyme karte hain, isse seedha yaad rakho ki is jeet se hi Patel ko \"Sardar\" mila.\n3. Santhal(Hul) vs Munda(Ulgulan) — Sabse Bada Trap\n●Santhal Rebellion(Hul,1855-56) = Sidhu & Kanhu · Bengal/Jharkhand · \"Hul\"(Santali) = \"revolt\"\n●Munda Rebellion(Ulgulan,1899-1900) = Birsa Munda · Jharkhand · \"Ulgulan\"(Mundari) = \"Great Tumult\"\n TRICK — \"Hul-Sidhu/Kanhu, Ulgulan-Birsa\" trick\n💡\n44 saal ka gap(1855→1899). Santhal = 2 bhai leaders(Sidhu+Kanhu), Munda = 1 leader(Birsa). \"Hul = Happens-\npehle(1855), Ulgulan = Us-baad(1899)\" — H before U alphabetically bhi, aur time mein bhi pehle.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSanthal Rebellion(Hul,1855-56)=Sidhu&Kanhu. Munda Rebellion(Ulgulan,1899-1900)=Birsa Munda.\n\"Hul\"=revolt(Santali). \"Ulgulan\"=Great Tumult(Mundari) — dono bilkul alag hain.\n4. Tebhaga(1946-47) — 2/3rd, NOT Half-Half\n●Tebhaga = 3 shares — sharecroppers ko 2/3rd, landlord ko sirf 1/3rd (pehle half-half tha)\n●Led by BPKS/All India Kisan Sabha(CPI) — Bengal\n TRICK — \"Tebhaga=Teen bhaag\" trick\n💡\nTebhaga = \"Teen bhaag\"(3 shares) — naam mein hi \"teen\" chhupa hai. Demand: 2 bhaag kisan ko, 1 bhaag zamindar\nko — pehle 1-1(half-half) tha, ab 2:1 ka naya ratio maanga gaya.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTebhaga demand = sharecroppers ko 2/3rd share (landlord ko sirf 1/3rd) — pehle half-half tha, half-half ko final answer\nmat samajhna.","5. Paika(1817) vs Sambalpur(1827-62) — Dono Odisha, Alag Leaders\n●Paika Rebellion(1817-25) = Bakshi Jagabandhu · land revenue+salt monopoly\n●Sambalpur Rebellion(1827-62) = Surendra Sai · alag/baad ka movement\n TRICK — \"Paika-Bakshi, Sambalpur-Surendra\" trick\n💡\nDono ODISHA mein hain isliye confuse hote hain — Paika-Bakshi(pehle,1817), Sambalpur-Surendra(baad mein,1827+,\nS-S bhi match karta hai) — same state, alag leader, alag decade.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPaika Rebellion(1817)=Bakshi Jagabandhu. Sambalpur Rebellion(1827-62)=Surendra Sai. Dono Odisha mein hain par\nbilkul ALAG movements/leaders.\n6. Indigo Movement(1859) vs Champaran(1917) — Dono Indigo, Alag Hain\n●Indigo Movement/Neel Vidroh(1859-60) = Digambar Biswas · Bengal · forced indigo cultivation\n●Champaran(1917) = Gandhi · Bihar · Tinkathia system\n TRICK — \"58-saal gap, alag state, alag leader\" trick\n💡\nDono \"indigo\" se related hain isliye confuse hote hain, par: Neel Vidroh(1859,Bengal,Digambar Biswas) vs\nChamparan(1917,Bihar,Gandhi) — 58 saal ka gap, alag state, alag leader — sirf \"crop\"(indigo) common hai, baaki\nsab alag.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIndigo Movement/Neel Vidroh(1859-60,Bengal,Digambar Biswas) ≠ Champaran(1917,Bihar,Gandhi) — dono indigo-\nrelated hain par 58 saal ka gap aur alag state/leader.\n7. Moplah Rebellion(1921-22) — 3 Causes, Ek Nahi\n●Khilafat Movement + Anti-Landlord + Anti-British — teeno saath, leader Ali Musliyar, Kerala\n TRICK — \"3-in-1\" trick\n💡\nMoplah = TEEN causes ek saath(Khilafat+Landlord+British) — koi bhi EK causes bolna incomplete hai. \"Moplah =\nMultiple(teen) causes\" — is completeness ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMoplah Rebellion(1921-22) ke 3 causes the: Khilafat Movement + Anti-Landlord + Anti-British — sirf ek causes batana\nincomplete answer hai.\n8. 2 Ranis — Naam Mein Rani, Regions Alag\n●Rani Chennamma = Kittur Rebellion(1824-29), Karnataka\n●Rani Gaidinliu = Naga Rebellion(1931), Nagaland(saath mein Jadonang)\n TRICK — \"Chennamma-South, Gaidinliu-Northeast\" trick\n💡\nChennamma = \"Chennai/South India\" jaisa sound(Karnataka). Gaidinliu = alag/exotic naam(Northeast/Nagaland) —\ndono \"Rani\" hain par region ki sound se hi distinguish karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRani Chennamma = Kittur Rebellion(Karnataka,1824-29). Rani Gaidinliu = Naga Rebellion(Nagaland,1931) — dono\nnaam mein \"Rani\" hai, mix mat karo.","9. Kuka vs Faraizi — Dono Religious-Reform, Alag Dharam\n●Kuka Movement(1860-70) = Bhagat Jawahar Mal · Punjab · Namdhari Sikh reform\n●Faraizi Movement(1818-60) = Haji Shariatullah · Bengal · Muslim reform\n TRICK — \"Kuka-Sikh, Faraizi-Muslim\" trick\n💡\nKuka = \"gurkul/Sikh\" jaisa sound(Punjab, Namdhari Sikh). Faraizi = \"Faraz/Islamic duty\" (Bengal, Muslim reform) —\nnaam se hi dharm-connect ho jaata hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Champaran(1917,1st,Bihar,indigo) vs Kheda(1918,Gujarat) → Bardoli(1928)=Sardar-Patel → Santhal-\nHul(1855,Sidhu+Kanhu) vs Munda-Ulgulan(1899,Birsa) → Tebhaga=2/3rd(not half-half) → Paika(1817,Bakshi) vs\nSambalpur(1827,Surendra Sai) → IndigoMovement(1859,Bengal,Digambar) vs Champaran(1917,Bihar,Gandhi) →\nMoplah=3causes(Khilafat+Landlord+British) → RaniChennamma(Kittur,Karnataka) vs RaniGaidinliu(Naga,Nagaland)\n→ Kuka(Sikh,Punjab) vs Faraizi(Muslim,Bengal)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Santhal(Hul,1855,Sidhu&Kanhu) ≠ Munda(Ulgulan,1899,Birsa Munda) — dono bilkul alag.\n2) Tebhaga = 2/3rd share sharecroppers ko (half-half NAHI, teen-bhaag ka naya ratio).\n3) Moplah Rebellion ke 3 causes: Khilafat+Anti-Landlord+Anti-British — sirf ek mat batana.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Peasant Movements & Tribal Revolts","SOCIO-RELIGIOUS REFORM MOVEMENTS — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nModern History · Chapter 5 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Raja Ram Mohan Roy — 2 Titles, 2 Sources\n●\"Raja\" = Mughal Emperor Akbar II ne diya\n●\"Yugdoot\" = Subhash Chandra Bose ne kaha(\"The Indian Struggle\" kitaab mein)\n●Anti-Sati Bill(1829) = Regulation XVII, William Bentinck ne sign kiya\n TRICK — \"Purana Raja, Naya Yugdoot\" trick\n💡\nRaja = PURANA/Mughal source(Akbar II, khud ek raja tha, isliye \"Raja\" title dene wala bhi raja hi tha — natural\nmatch). Yugdoot = NAYA/Modern source(Subhash Bose, 20th century leader) — \"purana title purane raja se, naya\ntitle naye leader se\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Raja\" title = Akbar II(Mughal Emperor) ne diya. \"Yugdoot\" = Subhash Chandra Bose ne kaha — dono alag sources\nhain, mix mat karo.\n2. Brahmo Samaj — Poora Timeline + Splits\n●1828: Brahmo Samaj(RMMR) → 1839: Tattvabodhini Sabha(Debendranath Tagore)\n●1866 GREAT SPLIT: Adi Brahmo Samaj(Debendranath) vs Indian Brahmo Samaj(Keshab Chandra Sen)\n●1878: Sadharan Brahmo Samaj(Keshab se DOBARA split)\n TRICK — \"Adi=Purana, Sadharan=Doosri baar\" trick\n💡\nAdi Brahmo = \"Adi\"(original/purana) — Debendranath, jo shuru se Samaj mein tha. Indian Brahmo = naya\ngroup — Keshab, jo baad mein aaya(1858) aur split kiya(1866). Sadharan = Keshab SE HI dobara split(1878) —\nmatlab Keshab ka group bhi khud aage jaake toota. Pattern: \"split-pe-split\", teen generations of division.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1866 Great Split: Adi Brahmo Samaj=Debendranath Tagore. Indian Brahmo Samaj=Keshab Chandra Sen. Sadharan\nBrahmo Samaj(1878)=Keshab se DOBARA split hua — teen-way division, sequence yaad rakho.\n3. Arya Samaj — Bombay Se Lahore Tak\n●Founded 1875, Bombay → HQ shift 1877, Lahore → DAV College bhi Lahore(1886)\n●Swami Dayanand Saraswati: \"Go back to the Vedas\" slogan · Satyarth Prakash(1874)\n TRICK — \"3 Lahore-links\" trick\n💡\nTeen cheezein Lahore se juda hai: HQ-shift(1877), DAV College(1886) — bas yaad rakho \"Arya Samaj Bombay\nmein PAIDA hui, Lahore mein BADI hui\" — origin alag, growth-center alag.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nArya Samaj founded 1875(Bombay), HQ shift 1877(Lahore). DAV College bhi Lahore mein(1886) — teeno Lahore-\nconnect, Bombay sirf founding-place hai.\n4. Theosophical Society — New York Mein Bani, India Mein NAHI\n●Founded 1875, NEW YORK(Blavatsky+Olcott) — India mein NAHI\n●India HQ = Adyar, Madras · Key India leader = Annie Besant(founder NAHI, later leader)","TRICK — \"New York=birth, Adyar=India-home\" trick\n💡\nTheosophical Society ka JANM New York mein hua(1875), phir India shift hui(Adyar) — jaise koi videshi\ncompany pehle apne desh mein bane, phir India mein branch khole. Annie Besant sirf India ki BRANCH ki leader\nthi, poore society ki founder NAHI.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTheosophical Society 1875 NEW YORK mein bani(Blavatsky+Olcott), India mein NAHI. Annie Besant = India-branch\nki leader, founder NAHI.\n5. Dharma Sabha(1830) — RMMR Ke KHILAF Thi\n●Radhakanta Dev(founder) → Orthodox organization → Sati ko SUPPORT kiya → RMMR ke reforms ke against\n TRICK — \"Dharma Sabha = Opposite team\" trick\n💡\nNaam \"Dharma Sabha\" sunke lagta hai koi reform group hoga — GALAT, ye RMMR ka VIRODHI(orthodox) group\ntha jo Sati ko SUPPORT karta tha. \"Dharma Sabha = Purani parampara ki team, RMMR = Naye reform ki team\"\n— dono opposite sides.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDharma Sabha(1830,Radhakanta Dev) = ORTHODOX group jo Sati ko support karta tha, RMMR ke reforms ke against\ntha — naam se confuse mat hona.\n6. AMU — College(1875) → University(1920)\n●Sir Syed Ahmed Khan → Muhammadan Anglo-Oriental College(1875) → baad mein AMU(1920)\n●Deoband(1866-67): Nanautavi+Gangohi → Abul Kalam Azad associated\n●Ahmadiyya(1889): Mirza Ghulam Ahmad, Punjab · Rahnumai Mazdayasan Sabha(1851): Dadabhai Naoroji(Parsi,\nIslam se related NAHI)\n TRICK — \"1875-College, 1920-University\" + \"Rahnumai=Parsi\" trick\n💡\nAMU ki DO dates: 1875(college banayi) → 1920(university ban gayi) — 45 saal ka gap, dono yaad rakho.\nRahnumai Mazdayasan Sabha naam Islamic lagta hai par ye PARSI reform movement hai(Dadabhai Naoroji) —\nis naam-trap ko yaad rakho, \"Mazdayasan\" khud Zoroastrianism se related word hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMuhammadan Anglo-Oriental College(1875) → AMU(1920). Rahnumai Mazdayasan Sabha(1851,Dadabhai Naoroji) =\nPARSI reform, Islam se related NAHI.\n7. Phule Couple & Vivekananda — Key Dates\n●Savitribai Phule = First Woman Teacher of India · 1848 school banaya\n●Jyotiba Phule: Gulamgiri(1872) — Satyashodhak Samaj(1873) se PEHLE likhi gayi\n●Vivekananda: birth 12 Jan 1863(=National Youth Day) · real naam Narendranath Dutta\n TRICK — \"Book pehle, Samaj baad mein\" + Birthday trick\n💡\nGulamgiri(1872) LIKHI GAYI Satyashodhak Samaj(1873) BANNE SE PEHLE — ek saal ka gap, book pehle aayi\nphir organization bani.\n12 January = Vivekananda ka birthday = National Youth Day(1984 se) — is double-meaning date ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nJyotiba Phule ki Gulamgiri(1872) Satyashodhak Samaj(1873) banne se PEHLE likhi gayi thi — order confuse mat karo.","8. Ranade \"Socrates of India\" + Narayana Guru's 3 Movements\n●M.G. Ranade = \"Socrates of India\" · Prarthana Samaj(1869 join) · Indian National Social Conference(1887,\"Social\nWing of INC\")\n●Shri Narayana Guru(Kerala) = 3 movements: Aravipuram(1888) → Temple Entry(1902) → SNDP Yogam(1902-03)\n TRICK — \"Ranade=Philosopher, Narayana Guru=Kerala-triple\" trick\n💡\nRanade = Socrates(Greek philosopher se comparison, uski wisdom/reasoning-based reform ke liye). Narayana Guru =\nKerala ka SABSE ACTIVE reformer, teen alag movements chalayi — \"ek nahi, TEEN\" yaad rakho, exam isi count pe\npakadta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nShri Narayana Guru = 3 movements(Aravipuram-1888, Temple Entry-1902, SNDP Yogam-1902-03) — Kerala ke sabse\nactive anti-untouchability reformer.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"RMMR: Raja(AkbarII)-Yugdoot(SubhashBose) → BrahmoSamaj: 1828-1839(Tattvabodhini)-1866(Split:Adi-\nDebendranath/Indian-Keshab)-1878(Sadharan) → AryaSamaj: Bombay1875→Lahore1877→DAV1886 →\nTheosophical: NewYork1875→Adyar(India-HQ) → DharmaSabha=orthodox,anti-RMMR → AMU:\ncollege1875→university1920 → Rahnumai=Parsi(not Islam) → Phule: Gulamgiri1872→SatyashodhakSamaj1873 →\nVivekananda=12Jan=NationalYouthDay → Ranade=SocratesOfIndia → NarayanaGuru=3movements(Kerala)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Theosophical Society NEW YORK mein bani(1875), India mein nahi — India HQ=Adyar hai.\n2) Dharma Sabha(1830) orthodox thi, RMMR ke against — naam se confuse mat hona.\n3) 1866 Split: Adi Brahmo=Debendranath. Indian Brahmo=Keshab. Sadharan(1878)=Keshab se dobara split.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Socio-Religious Reform Movements","PRESS & EDUCATION IN INDIA — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 6 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Press Ki Shuruaat — Firsts\n●Bengal Gazette(1780) = India ka PEHLA newspaper(English) — Editor James Augustus Hickey\n●Udant Martand(1826) = PEHLA Hindi newspaper\n●Printing Press: Portuguese(Goa,1557) → EIC(Mumbai,1674)\n TRICK — \"1780-Hickey, 1826-Hindi\" trick\n💡\n46 saal ka gap(1780→1826) — pehle overall newspaper(English,Hickey), phir 46 saal baad pehla HINDI newspaper.\n\"Hickey ka Hindi wala successor 46 saal baad aaya\" — is gap se dono dates lock ho jaati hain.\n2. 7 Press Acts — Chronological Sequence\n●1799 Wellesley(Censorship) → 1823 John Adams(Licensing) → 1835 Metcalfe(\"Liberator\") → 1857\nCanning(Licensing, Revolt ke time) → 1878 Lytton(Vernacular/\"Gagging\") → 1908+1910 Minto II(2 Acts)\n TRICK — \"Restrict-Restrict-FREE-Restrict-Restrict-Restrict×2\" trick\n💡\nPattern: sab acts RESTRICT karte hain, SIRF Metcalfe(1835) FREE karta hai — is ek alag rang ke act ko yaad\nrakho, baaki sab \"control\" ki taraf hain, Metcalfe akela \"freedom\" wala.\nMinto II = 2 Acts EK HI Viceroy ne(1908+1910) — koi aur Viceroy ne double-Act nahi kiya, ye uniqueness yaad\nrakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMetcalfe(1835) = \"Liberator of Press\"(freedom di). Vernacular Press Act(1878,Lytton) = \"Gagging Act\"(restrict kiya).\nMinto II ne 2 Acts pass kiye(1908+1910) — ek hi Viceroy.\n3. Amrit Bazar Patrika — Raatoraat Bengali Se English\n●1868 founded(Sisir Kumar Ghosh+Motilal Ghosh) → 1878 Vernacular Press Act se bachne ke liye 21 March 1878\nko Bengali se ENGLISH mein badal liya\n TRICK — \"Raatoraat bhasha badli\" trick\n💡\nVernacular Press Act sirf VERNACULAR(local-language) papers ko target karta tha, English EXEMPT thi —\nisliye ABP ne SMART move khela: bas bhasha badal di, publication band nahi ki. Ye poore chapter ka SABSE\nDRAMATIC/legendary moment hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAmrit Bazar Patrika ne Vernacular Press Act(1878) se bachne ke liye Bengali se English mein badal liya — kyunki Act\nsirf vernacular(local-language) papers cover karta tha.\n4. Macaulay's Minute(1835) vs Wood's Dispatch(1854)\n●Macaulay(1835) = \"Downward Filtration Theory\" — English medium, upper-class target\n●Wood's Dispatch(1854) = \"Magna Carta of Indian Education\" — GG Dalhousie · School=vernacular,\nCollege=English(dual policy)\n TRICK — \"Macaulay=Filter, Wood's=Magna Carta\" trick\n💡\nMacaulay = \"upar se neeche TAPKANA\"(filtration — sirf upper class ko English do, baaki tak \"chhan ke\" pahunche).\nWood's = \"Magna Carta\"(bada constitutional-jaisa document, DUAL policy — vernacular+English dono level pe). 19\nsaal ka gap(1835→1854), dono alag philosophy.","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMacaulay's Minute(1835) = Downward Filtration Theory(English-only,upper class). Wood's Dispatch(1854,Dalhousie)\n= Magna Carta of Indian Education(dual: school=vernacular, college=English) — do alag policies.\n5. 6 Education Commissions — Chairman + Key Reform\n●Hunter(1882-83,Ripon) = Wood's Dispatch review, Primary+Secondary focus\n●Indian University Commission(1904,Curzon) = Sir Thomas Raleigh, stricter control\n●Sadler(1917,Chelmsford) = M.E.Sadler → 12th(Intermediate) ko Degree se ALAG kiya\n●Hartog(1929,Irwin) = Philip Hartog → \"Wastage and Stagnation\"\n●Sargent Plan(1944) = Free+Compulsory Education(6-11 saal)\n●Radhakrishnan(1948) = 1st Education Commission of INDEPENDENT India → UGC ka base\n TRICK — \"HISHSR\" 6-commission trick\n💡\nHunter-IndianUniv-Sadler-Hartog-Sargent-Radhakrishnan = \"HISHSR\" — chronological order, British-era 5(Hunter se\nSargent) → phir AAKHRI(Radhakrishnan) Independence ke BAAD ka pehla — ye \"before/after independence\" split\nyaad rakho.\nSadler = 12th ALAG kiya(intermediate concept). Hartog = Wastage+Stagnation(dropout-focused). Dono naam se hi\nkaam yaad nahi aata, bas ratt lo: S-12th, H-Wastage.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRadhakrishnan Committee(1948) = 1ST Education Commission of INDEPENDENT India(UGC ka base). Sadler(1917)\n= 12th ko Degree se alag kiya. Hartog(1929) = Wastage and Stagnation.\n6. Major Institutions — Founder Match\n●Calcutta Madrasa(1781,Warren Hastings) = 1st Oriental Institution\n●Asiatic Society(1784,William Jones) · Banaras Sanskrit College(1791,Jonathan Duncan)\n●Hindu College(1817,RMMR+David Hare) · 3 Universities(1857) — SAME saal Revolt of 1857!\n●Central Hindu College(1898,Annie Besant) → baad mein BHU ban gaya\n TRICK — \"1857 coincidence\" trick\n💡\nCalcutta+Madras+Bombay Universities SAME SAAL bani jis saal Revolt of 1857 hui — is coincidence ko yaad\nrakho, exam isi angle se poochta hai: \"jis saal India ne British ke against ladi, usi saal British ne apna education-system\nbhi establish kiya\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n3 Universities(Calcutta,Madras,Bombay) 1857 mein bani — YEHI SAAL Revolt of 1857 ka bhi hai, coincidence yaad\nrakho.\n7. Journals & Books — Author Match Traps\n●Tilak: Kesari(Marathi) + Maratha(English) — 2 journals, 2 alag bhasha\n●Annie Besant: New India + Commonweal — 2 journals\n●Azad: Al-Hilal(journal,Urdu) + India Wins Freedom(book)\n●\"The Independent\" = Motilal Nehru(pita), Jawaharlal NAHI\n●\"Leader\": Founder=Malaviya, Editor=C.Y.Chintamani(alag roles)\n TRICK — \"Motilal not Jawaharlal\" + \"Founder≠Editor\" trick\n💡\n\"The Independent\" = MOTILAL(baap) — \"Jawaharlal\" hamesha option mein diya jaata hai but GALAT hai, yaad\nrakho \"baap ne shuru ki, bete ne nahi\".\n\"Leader\" journal ke 2 roles: Malaviya=Founder(shuru kiya), Chintamani=Editor(chalaya) — MCQ mein dono\noptions mein aa sakte hain, role dhyan se padho.","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"The Independent\" journal = Motilal Nehru ne banayi (Jawaharlal NAHI). \"Leader\" journal: Founder=Malaviya,\nEditor=C.Y.Chintamani — do alag roles.\n8. Valentine Chirol — 2 Cheezein Ek Hi Title\n●Valentine Chirol(British journalist,\"Indian Unrest\" book) ne DONO ko \"Father of Indian Unrest\" kaha: Tilak AUR\nArya Samaj\n TRICK — \"Ek title, do winners\" trick\n💡\nSame title EK VYAKTI(Tilak) aur EK ORGANIZATION(Arya Samaj) dono ko diya gaya — \"Chirol ne DO baar\nsame compliment/criticism diya\" — is duplication ko yaad rakho, exam dono options try karta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nValentine Chirol ne \"Father of Indian Unrest\" title DONO ko diya: Tilak(vyakti) AUR Arya Samaj(organization) —\ndono associations yaad rakho.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"BengalGazette(1780,Hickey)-UdantMartand(1826,Hindi) → PressActs: Wellesley1799-Adams1823-\nMetcalfe1835(Liberator)-Canning1857-Lytton1878(Gagging)-MintoII1908+1910 → ABP: Bengali→English(1878) →\nMacaulay1835(Filtration) vs Wood's1854(MagnaCarta,Dalhousie) → Commissions: HISHSR(Hunter-IndianUniv-\nSadler-Hartog-Sargent-Radhakrishnan) → Institutions: CalcuttaMadrasa1781-AsiaticSociety1784-HinduCollege1817-\n3Universities1857(=Revolt year) → Journals: Tilak(Kesari-Maratha),Besant(NewIndia-\nCommonweal),TheIndependent=MotilalNOTJawaharlal,Leader=Malaviya(founder)/Chintamani(editor) → Chirol:\nTilak+AryaSamaj dono='FatherOfIndianUnrest'\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) \"The Independent\" = Motilal Nehru(NOT Jawaharlal).\n2) Wood's Dispatch(1854)=Magna Carta of Education. Macaulay's Minute(1835)=Downward Filtration Theory — do\nalag policies.\n3) 3 Universities(Calcutta,Madras,Bombay) 1857 mein bani — Revolt of 1857 ke SAME saal.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Press & Education in India","FORMATION OF INDIAN NATIONAL CONGRESS — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 7 (High Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. INC Formation — 3 Theories, 3 Angle\n●Safety Valve Theory = A.O. Hume(British angle) — Indian gussa release karne ke liye\n●Lightning Conductor Theory = Gokhale(Indian angle) — Indians ne Hume ko istemal kiya\n●Conspiracy Theory = R.P. Dutt(Marxist/critical angle) — poori British saazish\n TRICK — \"3 alag chashme\" trick\n💡\n3 alag \"lens\" se dekha gaya: Hume(khud British) = apna hi bachaav(safety valve), Gokhale(Indian) = ulta\nangle(hum ne unhe use kiya), Dutt(Marxist) = sabse critical(conspiracy). \"Hume-Safety, Gokhale-Lightning, Dutt-\nConspiracy\" — H-S, G-L, D-C bolke ratt lo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSafety Valve Theory=Hume. Lightning Conductor Theory=Gokhale. Conspiracy Theory=R.P.Dutt — teeno alag angle\nse hain, mix mat karo.\n2. Pre-Congress Organizations — 2 \"Sabse\" Trap\n●Landholders' Society(1838,Dwarkanath Tagore) = India ka PEHLA Organized Political Association\n●Indian National Association(1876,Surendranath Banerjee) = SABSE IMPORTANT pre-Congress org — 1886 mein\nSEEDHA INC mein MERGE hui\n TRICK — \"Pehla≠Sabse Important\" trick\n💡\nLandholders' Society = TIME mein pehla(1838), Indian National Association = IMPORTANCE mein\npehla(1876,direct INC predecessor) — dono \"pehla\" hain par ALAG dimension mein: ek TIME-first, doosra\nIMPORTANCE-first(kyunki ye seedha INC mein hi merge ho gayi).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIndia ka PEHLA Organized Political Association = Landholders' Society(1838,Dwarkanath Tagore). SABSE\nIMPORTANT pre-Congress org = Indian National Association(1876, jo 1886 mein INC mein merge hui) — dono\nconfuse mat karo.\n3. Dadabhai Naoroji — Har Jagah Naam Aata Hai\n●Bombay Association(1852) + London India Society(1865) + East India Association(1866,London,SOLO founder)\n●Title: \"Grand Old Man of India\" · Drain of Wealth Theory · \"Swaraj\" shabd pehli baar use kiya(1906,22nd\nSession)\n TRICK — \"Naoroji = Har jagah\" trick\n💡\nNaoroji 3+ organizations mein involved tha — \"jahan bhi kuch shuru hua, wahan Naoroji zaroor tha\" — is\nomnipresence ko yaad rakho, isliye unhe \"Grand Old Man\" bhi kaha jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Swaraj\" shabd pehli baar Dadabhai NAOROJI ne use kiya(1906,22nd Session,Calcutta) — Gokhale ya Tilak ne NAHI.\n4. INC Founding — Core Facts\n●28 December 1885, Bombay(Gokuldas Tejpal Sanskrit College) · Founder A.O. Hume · 1st President W.C. Bonnerjee\n· Viceroy Lord Dufferin","●72 delegates — Bombay se max(38)\n TRICK — \"Founder≠President\" reminder\n💡\nHume(British) = FOUNDER, Bonnerjee(Indian) = 1ST PRESIDENT — do alag roles, do alag log — pattern jo\nbaar-baar dikha hai(jaise founder vs real-founder), yahan founder vs president.\n5. Vande Mataram(1896) vs Jana Gana Mana(1911) — Dono Calcutta\n●Vande Mataram: 12th Session(1896,Calcutta,President Sayani) · Composer Bankim Chandra(Anandamath,1882) ·\nSinger Rabindranath Tagore\n●Jana Gana Mana: 26th Session(1911,Calcutta,President Bishan Narayan Dhar) · Composer+Singer Rabindranath\nTagore(dono role khud)\n TRICK — \"12th vs 26th, dono Calcutta\" trick\n💡\nDono SAME CITY(Calcutta) mein hue, par 15 saal ka gap(1896→1911) — 12th session(chota number)=Vande\nMataram(purana), 26th session(bada number)=Jana Gana Mana(baad ka) — session-number se hi chronology\nyaad rakho.\nVande Mataram mein COMPOSER aur SINGER alag(Bankim+Tagore), Jana Gana Mana mein Tagore ne\nDONO kiya(khud likha, khud gaya) — ye role-difference yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nVande Mataram=12th Session(1896,Calcutta) — Composer Bankim Chandra, Singer Tagore(alag log). Jana Gana\nMana=26th Session(1911,Calcutta) — Tagore ne khud likha+gaya dono.\n6. Surat Split(1907) — President Yaad Rakho, Tilak NAHI\n●23rd Session, Surat, 1907 → President Rash Bihari Ghosh(Tilak ya Lal-Bal-Pal NAHI — wo sirf leaders the)\n●Moderates(Naram Dal) vs Extremists(Garam Dal) — 1906 ke 4 resolutions ko poore India mein failane ka mudda\n TRICK — \"Surat ki Surat bigdi\" trick(source ka mnemonic)\n💡\n\"Surat mein Congress ki Surat(shakal) bigad gayi\" — wordplay se hi Surat Split yaad rah jaata hai. President = Rash\nBihari Ghosh — Tilak famous hai isliye log usse president samajh lete hain, GALAT hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSurat Split(1907,23rd Session) ka PRESIDENT = Rash Bihari Ghosh — Tilak ya Lal-Bal-Pal NAHI (wo extremist\nleaders the, president nahi).\n7. 2 Female Presidents — 8 Saal Ka Gap\n●1917(32nd Session,Calcutta): Annie Besant = 1st Female President — VIDESHI(British)\n●1925(Kanpur): Sarojini Naidu = 1st INDIAN Female President\n TRICK — \"Besant-Videshi, Naidu-Desi\" trick\n💡\nBesant PEHLE(1917) par VIDESHI, Naidu BAAD mein(1925) par DESI — 8 saal ka gap. \"Besant = British(pehle),\nNaidu = Native(baad mein)\" — B-before-N bhi alphabetically match karta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1st Female President=Annie Besant(1917,videshi/British). 1st INDIAN Female President=Sarojini Naidu(1925,Kanpur)\n— 8 saal ka gap, dono alag categories.\n8. Gandhi — SIRF EK BAAR President\n●39th Session(1924,Belgaum,Karnataka) = Gandhi ji ki EKLAUTI presidency\n●Youngest President = Abul Kalam Azad(1923,Delhi Special Session)","●44th(1929,Lahore,Nehru) = Purna Swaraj resolution · 45th(1931,Karachi,Patel) = Fundamental Rights resolution\n TRICK — \"1924=ek baar\" trick\n💡\nGandhi itne bade leader the, par President SIRF EK BAAR bane(1924,Belgaum) — ye counter-intuitive fact\nhai(itna bada naam, itni kam baar president), isliye alag se yaad rakho: \"1924 = Gandhi ka EK-AUR-EKLAUTA\nsaal\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMahatma Gandhi SIRF EK BAAR INC President bane — 1924, Belgaum(Karnataka) session mein. Baaki kisi bhi saal\nnahi.\n9. Kisne Kya Kaha — Quote Match\n●Lord Dufferin(Viceroy) = \"Microscopic Minority\"\n●Lord Curzon(Viceroy) = \"Peaceful demise\" chahta tha\n●Bankim Chandra(writer) = \"padon ke bhookhe\"(hungry for positions)\n●Bipin Chandra Pal(extremist) = \"Petitioning Institution of Moderates\"\n TRICK — \"2 Viceroy + 2 Writer/Leader\" trick\n💡\n4 quotes, 2 categories: 2 VICEROYS(Dufferin+Curzon) = British-official criticism, 2 INDIAN(Bankim+BipinPal)\n= internal/extremist criticism — \"British bahar se critical, apne log andar se critical\" — dono taraf se Congress critique\nhui.\n10. Muslim League(1906) — 3 Alag Naam\n●Initiative: Nawab Salimullah(Dhaka) · 1st President: Aga Khan · HQ: Lucknow\n TRICK — \"Salimullah-Idea, AgaKhan-President, Lucknow-HQ\" trick\n💡\n3 alag roles, 3 alag jagah/naam: Salimullah = shuru KARANE wala(Dhaka), Aga Khan = LEAD karne wala(1st\npresident), Lucknow = sirf HQ(Dhaka mein bani thi, HQ alag city mein) — teeno mix mat karo, exam directly poochta\nhai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMuslim League(1906,Dhaka): Initiative=Nawab Salimullah. 1st President=Aga Khan. HQ=Lucknow — teeno alag facts\nhain, ek dusre se swap mat karo.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"3 theories: SafetyValve-Hume,LightningConductor-Gokhale,Conspiracy-Dutt → Pre-Congress:\nLandholdersSociety(1838,1st-ever) vs IndianNationalAssociation(1876,most-important,merged1886) → Naoroji: multi-\norg+Swaraj-word(1906) → INC: 28Dec1885,Hume-founder,Bonnerjee-1stPresident,Dufferin-viceroy →\nVandeMataram(1896,12th,Bankim+Tagore) vs JanaGanaMana(1911,26th,Tagore-both) →\nSuratSplit(1907,23rd,RashBihariGhosh) → Females: Besant(1917,videshi)-Naidu(1925,desi) → Gandhi=1924-\nBelgaum(only once) → Quotes: Dufferin-MicroscopicMinority,Curzon-PeacefulDemise,BipinPal-PetitioningInstitution\n→ MuslimLeague: Salimullah-initiative,AgaKhan-president,Lucknow-HQ\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGH-WEIGHTAGE chapter hai.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) 1st Female President=Besant(1917,videshi). 1st INDIAN Female=Sarojini Naidu(1925) — 8 saal ka gap.","2) \"Swaraj\" shabd pehli baar Dadabhai Naoroji ne use kiya(1906) — Gokhale/Tilak nahi.\n3) Surat Split(1907) ka President=Rash Bihari Ghosh, Tilak NAHI.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Formation of Indian National Congress","INDIAN NATIONAL MOVEMENT — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 8 (High Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Bengal Partition — 3 Alag Dates\n●Announced: 19 July 1905 · Effective: 16 October 1905 · Cancelled: 1911(Delhi Durbar, Lord Hardinge II)\n●Viceroy jisne partition kiya = Curzon(Divide&Rule) · Viceroy jisne cancel kiya = Hardinge II(alag vyakti)\n TRICK — \"Announce-Effective-Cancel\" 3-stage trick\n💡\nJulai mein Announce, October mein Effective(3 mahine gap, same saal 1905), 1911 mein Cancel(6 saal baad, alag\nViceroy) — teen stage: \"ghoshna→lagu→radd\", teen alag dates ek hi event ke.\nCurzon ne kiya, Hardinge II ne khatam kiya — do alag Viceroy, is symmetry ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBengal Partition: Announced(19 Jul 1905)→Effective(16 Oct 1905)→Cancelled(1911,Hardinge II) — teen alag dates,\nCurzon ne partition kiya par Hardinge II ne cancel kiya.\n2. 16 October 1905 — Ek Din, Do Ulti Reactions\n●Day of Mourning(shok) — poore Bengal mein\n●Rakhi Day(unity) — Rabindranath Tagore ke kehne par\n TRICK — \"Shok + Rakhi, same din\" trick\n💡\nEk hi din DONO opposite emotions manaye gaye — dukh(mourning) AUR ekta(rakhi) SAATH-SAATH — is\nunique double-reaction ko yaad rakho, ye chapter ka most-asked \"same day\" fact hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n16 October 1905 ko EK HI DIN Day of Mourning(shok) AUR Rakhi Day(Tagore ke kehne par unity) DONO manaye\ngaye.\n3. Mitra Mela(1899) → Abhinav Bharat(1904) — EK HI Organization\n●Mitra Mela(1899,Savarkar) ka naam 1904 mein badalkar Abhinav Bharat kar diya gaya\n●Inspiration: Mazzini ki \"Young Italy\"\n TRICK — \"Naam badla, organization wahi\" trick\n💡\n2 ALAG organizations NAHI hain — sirf EK hi hai jiska naam 5 saal baad badla. \"Mitra(dost) se Abhinav(naya)\nban gaya\" — dosti se naya-Bharat tak ka safar, ek hi group.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMitra Mela(1899) aur Abhinav Bharat(1904) DO ALAG organizations NAHI hain — Mitra Mela ka hi naam badla\ngaya, ek hi group hai(Savarkar brothers).\n4. Anushilan Samiti vs Dhaka Anushilan Samiti — Founder Alag\n●Anushilan Samiti(1902,Calcutta) = P. Mitra(Pramathanath Mitra) — \"Blood for Blood\"\n●Dhaka Anushilan Samiti(1905,Dhaka) = Pulin Das(P.Mitra se inspired, par SEPARATE branch, ~500 sub-branches)\n TRICK — \"Mitra=Calcutta, Das=Dhaka\" trick\n💡\nMitra-Calcutta(pehla,1902), Das-Dhaka(baad mein,1905, inspired-by-Mitra par SEPARATE) — M-C aur D-D dono\npairs first-letter match karte hain, isse yaad rakho.","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAnushilan Samiti(1902,Calcutta)=P.Mitra. Dhaka Anushilan Samiti(1905,Dhaka)=Pulin Das(inspired by Mitra, par\nseparate organization,~500 branches) — founders confuse mat karo.\n5. Muzaffarpur Bomb Case(1908) — Target ≠ Victim\n●Target: D.H. Kingsford(Judge) — par bomb GALTI SE Kennedy ki gaadi par gira, Kingsford BACH GAYA\n●Khudiram Bose: arrest+phaansi(11 Aug 1908, ~18 saal, youngest hanged revolutionary)\n●Prafulla Chaki: pakde jaane se pehle khud ko goli maar li(suicide)\n TRICK — \"Target-Kingsford, Victim-Kennedy\" trick\n💡\nAsli TARGET Kingsford tha, par galti se KENNEDY ki gaadi pe bomb gira — Kingsford is ghatna mein BACH\nGAYA. \"Kingsford Khatam nahi hua, Kennedy ki gaadi mein hui ghalti\" — dono \"K\" naam se confuse hota hai, target-\nvictim alag rakho.\nKhudiram = phaansi(caught+executed), Chaki = suicide(khud maara) — do alag ends, do alag revolutionaries.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMuzaffarpur Bomb Case: TARGET=Kingsford(Judge), par bomb galti se KENNEDY ki gaadi par gira — Kingsford\nbach gaya. Khudiram Bose=phaansi. Prafulla Chaki=suicide.\n6. Nasik Conspiracy(1909) vs Alipore Conspiracy(1908)\n●Nasik(1909): Jackson(Magistrate) ki hatya → Anant Laxman Kanhere(shooter, phaansi 1911) → Savarkar ko Kaala\nPani\n●Alipore(1908): 34 arrested, approver Narendra Gosain ko jail mein Kanailal Dutt+Satyendranath Bose ne maara ·\nAurobindo Ghosh acquitted → sanyas\n TRICK — \"Nasik-Jackson, Alipore-Gosain\" trick\n💡\nNasik = ek naya victim(Jackson), Alipore = andar hi ek TRAITOR maara gaya(Gosain, approver) — Nasik mein\nbahar ke officer ki hatya, Alipore mein jail ke ANDAR apne hi group ke traitor ki hatya. Bilkul alag nature ke cases.\nAlipore ke baad Aurobindo ne SANYAS liya(spiritual life, Puducherry Ashram-1926, Karmayogin-1909 newspaper)\n— is life-transformation ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNasik Conspiracy(1909)=Jackson ki hatya(Kanhere). Alipore Conspiracy(1908)=34 arrests, approver Gosain jail mein\nmaara gaya, Aurobindo Ghosh acquitted — dono ALAG cases.\n7. Revolutionaries Abroad — Country-Wise Match\n●India House(London,1905) = Shyamji Krishna Varma · Madan Lal Dhingra ne yahin se inspire hoke Curzon Wyllie\nko maara(1909)\n●Paris India Society(1905) = Madam Bhikaji Cama+S.R.Rana · Stuttgart(1907) mein PEHLA Tricolour fehraya\n●Ghadar Party(1913,San Francisco) = Founder Lala Hardayal, President Sohan Singh Bhakna(ALAG log)\n TRICK — \"London-Varma, Paris-Cama, Ghadar-2roles\" trick\n💡\n3 alag desh, 3 alag founder: London=Varma, Paris=Cama, USA=Hardayal(founder)+Bhakna(president) — USA\nwale mein DO log hain(founder≠president), baaki dono mein ek-ek.\nMadam Cama = \"Mother of Indian Revolution\" — Stuttgart mein Tiranga fehrane wali PEHLI, is \"first\" ko yaad\nrakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGhadar Party(1913,San Francisco): Founder=Lala Hardayal. President=Sohan Singh Bhakna — DO ALAG log, exam\nmein swap karke poochha jaata hai.","8. Home Rule Leagues — Bombay City Ka Trap\n●Tilak's League(Apr 1916,Pune) = President Joseph Baptista · Area: Karnataka+CP+Berar+Maharashtra EXCEPT\nBombay City\n●Besant's League(Sep 1916,Madras/Adyar) = Secretary George Arundale · Area: Rest of India INCLUDING Bombay\nCity\n TRICK — \"Tilak-NO Bombay, Besant-YES Bombay\" trick\n💡\nTilak Maharashtra ka hi leader tha, phir bhi BOMBAY CITY uske area mein NAHI thi — ye counter-intuitive\nfact hai isliye SABSE COMMON trap hai. Yaad rakho: \"Apne hi ghar(Maharashtra) mein Tilak ko Bombay City\nnahi mili, Besant(Madras se) ko mil gayi\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBombay City = Annie Besant's League ke area mein aati thi(Tilak's League mein NAHI, chahe Tilak khud Maharashtra\nka tha) — ye sabse common exam trap hai.\n9. Delhi Durbar(1911) — Announcement ≠ Official Shift\n●12 Dec 1911 = King George V welcome + Partition CANCEL + Capital-shift ANNOUNCEMENT(Lord Hardinge II)\n●Delhi OFFICIALLY capital = 1912(agle saal)\n TRICK — \"1911-Announce, 1912-Official\" trick\n💡\n1 saal ka gap: 1911 mein sirf GHOSHNA hui, 1912 mein ASLI/OFFICIAL shift hui — \"pehle bola gaya, agle saal hua\"\n— is 1-year-gap ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDelhi capital-shift ki ANNOUNCEMENT 1911(Delhi Durbar) mein hui, par Delhi OFFICIALLY capital 1912 mein\nbani — 1911 ko hi \"official\" mat samajhna.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"BengalPartition: 19Jul(announce)-16Oct(effective,mourning+rakhi)-1911(cancel,Hardinge) →\nMitraMela1899→AbhinavBharat1904(same org) → AnushilanSamiti(1902,Mitra,Calcutta) vs\nDhakaAnushilan(1905,PulinDas) → Muzaffarpur: target-Kingsford,hit-Kennedy,Khudiram-hanged,Chaki-suicide →\nNasik(1909,Jackson,Kanhere) vs Alipore(1908,34arrested,Gosain-killed,Aurobindo-acquitted) → Abroad: London-\nShyamjiVarma,Paris-MadamCama(Stuttgart1907),Ghadar-Hardayal(founder)/Bhakna(president) → HomeRule:\nTilak(Pune,NO-Bombay) vs Besant(Madras,YES-Bombay) → DelhiDurbar1911(announce)→1912(official)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGH-WEIGHTAGE chapter hai.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Bombay City = Besant's League mein(Tilak's League mein NAHI, chahe Tilak Maharashtra ka tha).\n2) Muzaffarpur: target Kingsford tha, bomb galti se Kennedy ki gaadi pe gira.\n3) Ghadar Party: Founder=Hardayal, President=Sohan Singh Bhakna — do alag log.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Indian National Movement","GANDHIAN ERA — FIRST PHASE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 9 (High Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 3 Early Satyagrahas — Har Ek Ka Apna \"First\"\n●Champaran(1917,Bihar) = 1st Civil Disobedience · Bulaya Rajkumar Shukla(sirf bulane wala,leader NAHI) ne\n●Ahmedabad(1918) = 1st Hunger Strike · Plague Bonus issue · 35% bonus mila\n●Kheda(1918,Gujarat) = 1st Asahyog(Non-cooperation) PRAYOG(experiment) · Patel ne bulaya\n TRICK — \"3 Firsts, 3 Alag Weapons\" trick\n💡\nChamparan = Disobedience(seedha inkaar), Ahmedabad = Hunger Strike(khud ko bhookha rakhna), Kheda =\nNon-cooperation(saath na dena) — teen alag \"weapon\", teen alag \"1st\" — bas yaad rakho ye TEENO alag category ke\n\"pehle\" hain, ek dusre se overlap nahi karte.\nRajkumar Shukla = SIRF BULANE WALA tha, team leader nahi(team = Rajendra Prasad+Kripalani+Mahadev\nDesai) — is role-distinction ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChamparan=1st Civil Disobedience. Ahmedabad=1st Hunger Strike. Kheda=1st Non-cooperation experiment — teeno\nalag \"firsts\", mix mat karo. Rajkumar Shukla sirf Gandhi ko BULANE wala tha, team-leader nahi.\n2. \"Mahatma\" Title & Indian Women's Association — Alag-Alag Log\n●\"Mahatma\" title = Rabindranath Tagore(post-Champaran) ne diya — Gokhale NAHI(wo political GURU the, title-\ngiver nahi)\n●Indian Women's Association(1917) = Annie Besant + Margaret Cousins ne banayi — Gandhi NAHI(1917 hone se\nconfuse hota hai, kyunki Champaran bhi 1917 hai)\n TRICK — \"1917 mein 2 alag events\" trick\n💡\n1917 saal mein DO alag cheezein hui: Champaran-safalta(Gandhi) → Mahatma title(Tagore) AUR Indian Women's\nAssociation(Besant) — same year hai isliye confuse hota hai, par teeno alag log/events. \"Same saal, alag kahaniyan\"\nyaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Mahatma\" title = Tagore ne diya(Gokhale nahi). Indian Women's Association(1917) = Annie Besant+Margaret Cousins\nne banayi(Gandhi nahi) — dono common galtiyaan hain.\n3. Rowlatt Act(1919) — Resignations Kahan Se?\n●\"Black Act\" · Slogan \"No Dalil, No Vakil, No Appeal\" · Committee Sidney Rowlatt(1917 bani)\n●Resignations: Malaviya+Mazharul Haq+Jinnah ne CENTRAL LEGISLATURE se resign kiya — Viceroy's Council\nSE NAHI\n TRICK — \"Legislature≠Council\" trick\n💡\nYe 3 leaders ne Central LEGISLATURE se resign kiya — Viceroy's COUNCIL se(jo baad mein Shankaran Nair ne\nkiya, Jallianwala ke context mein) confuse mat karo. Rowlatt = Legislature, Jallianwala = Council — do alag protests,\ndo alag bodies.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRowlatt Act ke against Malaviya+Mazharul Haq+Jinnah ne CENTRAL LEGISLATURE se resign kiya — Viceroy's\nExecutive COUNCIL se NAHI (wo Shankaran Nair ne, Jallianwala Bagh ke against).","4. Jallianwala Bagh — 3 Alag Reactions(MOST IMPORTANT)\n●Rabindranath Tagore = Knighthood(\"Sir\") LAUTAYI\n●Mahatma Gandhi = \"Kaiser-i-Hind\" title SURRENDER kiya\n●Shankaran Nair = Viceroy's Executive COUNCIL se RESIGN kiya\n TRICK — \"3 log, 3 alag protest-style\" trick\n💡\nTagore = TITLE(Knighthood) lautayi(honorary British title), Gandhi = TITLE(Kaiser-i-Hind) surrender\nkiya(WWI ke liye mila tha), Nair = POSITION(Council seat) chhodi(active role tha) — teeno alag TAREEKE se\nprotest kiya: 2 ne title choda, 1 ne position choda. Source khud isse \"MOST IMPORTANT MCQ\" bolta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nJallianwala Bagh ke baad: Tagore=Knighthood lautayi. Gandhi=Kaiser-i-Hind surrender kiya. Shankaran Nair=Viceroy's\nExecutive Council se resign kiya — teeno alag reactions, exam ka MOST IMPORTANT MCQ.\n5. Khilafat Movement — Start Aur End\n●All India Khilafat Conference(Nov 1919,Delhi) — President GANDHI(Hindu-Muslim unity ka \"sunehra mauka\")\n●Khilafat Day: 31 Aug 1920\n●End(1924): Mustafa Kemal Pasha ne Turkey mein reforms laaye(Caliphate abolish) → movement khud-ba-khud\nkhatam\n TRICK — \"Turkey ke andar ka reform, India ke movement ka end\" trick\n💡\nKhilafat Movement ISLIYE khatam hui kyunki TURKEY KHUD ne apna Caliphate system hata diya — jis cheez ke\nliye India mein movement chal rahi thi, wahi cheez Turkey ne khud khatam kar di. \"Jis Khalifa ko bachana tha,\nTurkey ne khud usko hata diya\" — is irony se end-reason yaad rakho.\n6. NCM — 2 Sessions, C.R. Das Ka U-Turn\n●Calcutta Special Session(Sep 1920): President Lala Lajpat Rai · C.R.Das = OPPOSE(proposal narrowly pass hua)\n●Nagpur Session(Dec 1920): President C.Vijayaraghavachariar · C.R.Das = KHUD move kiya(SUPPORT) → 15-\nmember CWC bani\n TRICK — \"Calcutta-Na, Nagpur-Haan\" trick\n💡\nC.R. Das ne 180-degree U-TURN liya: Calcutta mein \"NA\"(oppose) → Nagpur mein \"HAAN\"(khud propose) — 3\nmahine mein poora ulta stance, isliye ye TRAP-05 hai source mein bhi. \"Calcutta = Cold(opposed), Nagpur = New-\nmind(supported)\" — C-cold, N-new dono \"C/N\" se.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nC.R. Das ne Calcutta Session(1920) mein NCM proposal OPPOSE kiya, par Nagpur Session(1920) mein KHUD move\nkiya(support) — same saal, alag sessions, alag stance.\n7. NCM Start(1 Aug 1920) = Tilak Death — SAME DIN\n●1 August 1920 SUBAH: Tilak ki death → usi din NCM shuru hui\n●Tilak Swaraj Fund(1921): 6 mahine mein 1 Crore rupaye jama\n TRICK — \"Ek yug khatam, doosra shuru\" trick\n💡\nJis din \"Lal-Bal-Pal\" ke Tilak(Extremist era) ki maut hui, usi din Gandhi ka NCM(Mass Movement era) shuru\nhua — jaise ek era doosre ko baton pass kar raha ho, symbolically bhi perfect coincidence hai isliye exam mein bahut\npoocha jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1 August 1920 = NCM start date AUR Tilak death date, DONO SAME DIN — ye coincidence bahut common exam\nquestion hai.","8. Chauri-Chaura(4 Feb 1922) → Bardoli Resolution(12 Feb 1922)\n●Chauri-Chaura(Gorakhpur,UP): bheed ne police station mein aag lagayi → 22 policemen zinda jal gaye\n●Bardoli Resolution(12 Feb): NCM SUSPEND — sirf 8 din baad\n●Gandhi's quote: \"Himalayan Blunder\" · Bose's quote: \"National Calamity\"\n TRICK — \"Gandhi vs Bose\" contrasting-quote trick\n💡\nGandhi(jisne decision liya) = apni hi galti maani(\"Himalayan Blunder\" — khud ki galti). Bose(jo disagree tha) =\nmovement wapas lene ko hi galti bola(\"National Calamity\" — Gandhi ke decision ki criticism). Dono\n\"blunder/calamity\" negative words hain, par POINT OF VIEW alag: Gandhi apne upar, Bose Gandhi ke decision par.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Himalayan Blunder\" = Gandhi ne khud NCM wapas lene ke context mein apni galti maani. \"National Calamity\" =\nSubhash Chandra Bose ne NCM wapas lene ko criticize karte hue kaha — dono alag log, alag angle.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Gandhi India-wapas(9Jan1915) → 3 Satyagrahas: Champaran(1917,1stCivilDisobedience,Shukla-bulaya)-\nAhmedabad(1918,1stHungerStrike)-Kheda(1918,1stAsahyog) → Mahatma-title=Tagore(not Gokhale),\nIndianWomensAssoc=Besant(not Gandhi) → RowlattAct(1919,BlackAct): Malaviya+MazharulHaq+Jinnah resign-\nLEGISLATURE → JallianwalaBagh(13Apr1919): Tagore-Knighthood,Gandhi-KaiserIHind,ShankaranNair-\nCOUNCIL(3 alag) → Khilafat(Nov1919-Gandhi president,end1924-MustafaKemalPasha) → NCM:\nCalcuttaSession(Das-oppose)→NagpurSession(Das-support,CWC) → NCMstart(1Aug1920)=TilakDeath(same din) →\nChauriChaura(4Feb1922,22police)→BardoliResolution(12Feb1922) →\nGandhi='HimalayanBlunder',Bose='NationalCalamity'\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGH-WEIGHTAGE chapter hai.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Jallianwala reactions: Tagore=Knighthood, Gandhi=Kaiser-i-Hind, Shankaran Nair=Council — MOST\nIMPORTANT MCQ.\n2) C.R. Das: Calcutta Session=oppose, Nagpur Session=support — U-turn same saal mein.\n3) \"Mahatma\" title=Tagore(not Gokhale). \"Himalayan Blunder\"=Gandhi, \"National Calamity\"=Bose.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Gandhian Era — First Phase","PHASE OF NATIONAL POLITICS (1922–29) — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nModern History · Chapter 10 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Swaraj Party — No-Changers vs Pro-Changers\n●No-Changers: Rajagopalachari+Vallabhbhai Patel → Constructive work(schools,ashrams), council-entry ke KHILAF\n●Pro-Changers/Swarajists: C.R.Das(President)+Motilal Nehru(Secretary) → Council mein GHUSKE obstruct karna\n●Founded Jan 1923, Prayagraj · Earlier naam: Congress-Khilafat Swaraj Party\n TRICK — \"No=Bahar, Pro=Andar\" trick\n💡\nNo-Changers = \"NO to council\"(bahar rehke kaam karo, ashram/school). Pro-Changers = \"PRO council-\nentry\"(andar ghuso, obstruct karo) — naam mein hi seedha \"haan/na\" chhupa hai council-entry ke liye.\n2. Vitthalbhai vs Vallabhbhai Patel — 2 Bhai, 2 Alag Kaam\n●Vitthalbhai Patel(BADE bhai) = 1925, Speaker/President of Central Legislative Assembly(Swarajists ki sabse badi\njeet)\n●Vallabhbhai Patel(CHOTE bhai) = \"Sardar\" — Bardoli Satyagraha, No-Changer\n TRICK — \"Vit=Vidhan(Assembly), Val=Bardoli\" trick\n💡\nVitthalbhai = \"Vitthal jaisa BADA/senior naam\" → Assembly ka Speaker(bada legislative role). Vallabhbhai =\n\"Valiant Bardoli warrior\" → grassroots movement(Sardar title). Dono bhai hain, naam bhi milte-julte(Vit vs Val) —\nisliye SABSE COMMON trap, roles se differentiate karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nVitthalbhai Patel(bade bhai) = 1925 mein Speaker of Central Legislative Assembly. Vallabhbhai Patel(chote bhai) =\n\"Sardar\", Bardoli Satyagraha — dono bhai, roles bilkul alag.\n3. AITUC(1920) vs INTUC(1947) — Alag Union, Alag President\n●AITUC(1920): 1st President Lala Lajpat Rai · Split 1929(Nagpur,Nehru presided)\n●INTUC(May 1947): Founders Vallabhbhai Patel+V.V.Giri · 1st President Vallabhbhai Patel\n TRICK — \"AITUC-Lala, INTUC-Vallabhbhai\" trick\n💡\n27 saal ka gap(1920→1947) — AITUC = Lala Lajpat Rai(purana, pre-independence union), INTUC = Vallabhbhai\nPatel(naya, independence ke around ka union) — do alag unions, do alag \"1st President\", mix mat karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAITUC(1920) 1st President=Lala Lajpat Rai. INTUC(1947) 1st President=Vallabhbhai Patel — dono ALAG trade\nunions hain.\n4. CPI — 2 Formation Dates(\"Dates Ka Jhol\")\n●Abroad(Tashkent,Uzbekistan): 17 Oct 1920 · M.N.Roy\n●India mein(Kanpur): 26 Dec 1925 · Satyabhakta(presided)\n TRICK — \"Where dekho, date decide hogi\" trick\n💡\nSawaal ka wording padho: \"bahar/abroad\" → 1920,Tashkent,Roy. \"India mein\" → 1925,Kanpur,Satyabhakta. 5 saal\nka gap, do alag jagah — location-keyword hi answer decide karta hai.","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCPI abroad(Tashkent) = 17 Oct 1920, M.N.Roy. CPI India mein(Kanpur) = 26 Dec 1925, Satyabhakta — sawaal ka\n\"where\" dekho, wahi date decide karega.\n5. HRA → HSRA — Naam Badla, \"Socialist\" Add Hua\n●HRA(1924,Kanpur) = Sachindranath Sanyal · Objective: Armed Revolution, Federal Republic\n●HSRA(10 Dec 1928,Feroz Shah Kotla,Delhi) = Azad+Bhagat Singh · \"Socialist\" add hua\n TRICK — \"4-saal-baad Socialist add\" trick\n💡\nHRA se HSRA — EK HI organization ka EVOLUTION(naam badla), 2 alag groups NAHI — jaise Mitra\nMela→Abhinav Bharat pattern(Ch.8 se). \"Hindustan Republican(1924) → Hindustan SocialistRepublican(1928)**\" —\nbas beech mein \"Socialist\" add hua, 4 saal baad.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHRA(1924,Sanyal,Kanpur) aur HSRA(1928,Azad+Bhagat,Delhi) DO ALAG organizations NAHI — HRA ka hi naam\nbadalkar HSRA bana, \"Socialist\" word add hua.\n6. Saunders Assassination(17 Dec 1928) — Target ≠ Victim\n●Lala Lajpat Rai ki death(17 Nov 1928) — James Scott ke lathi-charge se\n●Asal TARGET = James Scott, par galti se John Saunders(Assistant SP) MAARA GAYA\n●Revolutionaries: Bhagat Singh+Azad+Rajguru\n TRICK — \"Scott-target, Saunders-victim\" trick(same pattern as Muzaffarpur)\n💡\nYe BILKUL WAHI PATTERN hai jo Muzaffarpur Bomb Case(Ch.8) mein tha — \"target ek(Kingsford/Scott), maara\ndoosra(Kennedy/Saunders)\" — dono chapters mein mistaken-identity ka fact hai, cross-verify karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSaunders assassination: ASAL TARGET James Scott tha(Lalaji ke lathi-charge order dene wala), par galti se John\nSaunders maara gaya.\n7. Assembly Bomb(8 Apr 1929) — 2 Bills, Ek Nahi\n●Bhagat Singh+Batukeshwar Dutt → Public Safety Bill + Trade Disputes Bill DONO ke against\n●Intention: \"To make the deaf hear\" — kisi ko maarna nahi tha\n TRICK — \"2 bills\" trick\n💡\nDO Bills tha protest ka reason, sirf ek mat batana — \"Public Safety AUR Trade Disputes, dono ek saath\" — jaise\nMoplah ke 3 causes(Ancient/Modern cross-pattern), yahan bhi COMPLETENESS zaroori hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAssembly Bomb Incident(1929) ka protest DO bills ke against tha: Public Safety Bill + Trade Disputes Bill — sirf ek\nbatana incomplete hai.\n8. 3 Alag Martyrdom Dates — Confuse Mat Ho\n●Jatin Das: 64-din hunger strike → death 13 Sep 1929\n●Chandrashekhar Azad: 27 Feb 1931, Alfred Park(Prayagraj) → khud ko goli mari, PHAANSI NAHI hui\n●Bhagat Singh+Sukhdev+Rajguru: 23 March 1931(Shaheed Diwas) → PHAANSI hui\n TRICK — \"3 alag deaths, 3 alag tareeke\" trick\n💡","Jatin Das = BHOOKH se(hunger strike,Sep1929), Azad = KHUD GOLI mari(Feb1931,phaansi NAHI), Bhagat-\nSukhdev-Rajguru = PHAANSI(Mar1931) — teen alag deaths, teen alag tareeke, teen alag mahine — is\nsequence(Sep→Feb→Mar) ko yaad rakho.\nAzad AUR Shaheed-Diwas-trio dono 1931 mein hain, par SIRF EK MAHINE ka gap(27Feb→23Mar) — Azad\nthodi der pehle mara, phir baaki teen ki phaansi hui.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChandrashekhar Azad(27 Feb 1931) ne KHUD ko goli mari, unhe PHAANSI NAHI hui — Shaheed Diwas(23 Mar\n1931,Bhagat Singh+Sukhdev+Rajguru) mein PHAANSI hui. Do alag tareeke, ek mahine ka gap.\n9. Journals — Bande Mataram ≠ New India\n●Bande Mataram = Bipin Chandra Pal\n●New India = Annie Besant(alag journal, alag vyakti)\n●Bandi Jivan = Sanyal ki book, \"Bible of Revolutionaries\"\n TRICK — \"Bande vs New\" trick\n💡\nBande Mataram(purana/nationalist slogan-jaisa naam) = Bipin Pal, New India(\"new\" word hi modern-sounding)\n= Annie Besant — naam ke \"feel\" se hi authors alag pakad lo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBande Mataram(journal) = Bipin Chandra Pal ka hai. New India = Annie Besant ka hai — dono alag journals, exam\nmein swap karke poochha jaata hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Gaya1922(CRDas proposal reject)→SwarajParty(Jan1923,Prayagraj,Das-President/MotilalNehru-Secretary) → No-\nChangers(Rajagopalachari+Vallabhbhai) vs Pro-Changers(Das+MotilalNehru) → Vitthalbhai(1925,Speaker) vs\nVallabhbhai(Sardar,Bardoli) → AITUC1920(LalaLajpatRai) vs INTUC1947(VallabhbhaiPatel) → CPI:\nTashkent1920(Roy) vs Kanpur1925(Satyabhakta) → HRA1924(Sanyal)→HSRA1928(Azad+Bhagat,renamed) →\nSaunders(17Dec1928,target-Scott,killed-Saunders) → AssemblyBomb(8Apr1929,2bills) →\nJatinDas(13Sep1929,64days) → Azad(27Feb1931,self-shot) → ShaheedDiwas(23Mar1931,Bhagat-Sukhdev-Rajguru)\n→ BandeMataram-BipinPal vs NewIndia-Besant\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Vitthalbhai(1925,Speaker CLA) vs Vallabhbhai(Sardar,Bardoli) — do bhai, alag roles.\n2) Azad(27Feb1931,khud goli mari,phaansi nahi) ≠ Bhagat-Sukhdev-Rajguru(23Mar1931,phaansi hui,Shaheed Diwas).\n3) CPI: Tashkent(1920,abroad,Roy) vs Kanpur(1925,India,Satyabhakta) — sawaal ka \"where\" dekho.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Phase of National Politics (1922-29)","GANDHIAN ERA — SECOND PHASE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 11 (Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Simon Commission — Poori TARAH British\n●7 members, SAARE British(koi Indian nahi) · Appointed Lord Birkenhead · Chairman Sir John Simon\n●Madras Session(27 Dec 1927): President M.A. Ansari(Nehru NAHI) → complete boycott decision\n TRICK — \"7-British, Ansari-not-Nehru\" trick\n💡\nSimon Commission mein EK BHI Indian nahi tha — isliye \"Simon Go Back\" naara laga. Madras Session ka\npresident ANSARI tha, chahe Nehru active role mein tha — \"active-hona\" aur \"president-hona\" alag baatein hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCongress Madras Session(1927) ka president M.A. Ansari tha — Jawaharlal Nehru NAHI(wo active tha par president\nnahi).\n2. Nehru Report(1928) — Motilal, NOT Jawaharlal\n●Chairman = MOTILAL Nehru(baap) — Jawaharlal ka NAHI\n●Muslim League(Jinnah) ne REJECT kiya → Jinnah ne apni \"14 Points\" di\n TRICK — \"Baap ki report\" trick\n💡\nYe BILKUL WAHI PATTERN hai jo \"The Independent\" journal(Ch.6) mein tha — \"Motilal(baap) = famous cheez ka\ncredit, Jawaharlal(beta) nahi\" — dono cross-chapter examples yaad rakho, ek hi family-trap pattern.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNehru Report(1928) = MOTILAL Nehru(chairman), Jawaharlal Nehru NAHI — baap-bete dono famous hain, alag karo.\n3. Dandi March — 3 Alag Dates\n●12 March 1930: START(Sabarmati Ashram, 78 followers)\n●5 April 1930: Dandi PAHUNCHE(24 din baad)\n●6 April 1930: Namak todkar CDM officially START\n TRICK — \"Start-Reach-Break\" 3-stage trick\n💡\n24 din CHALNA(12Mar→5Apr) → ek din baad KANOON TODNA(6Apr) — teen alag stages: safar-shuru →\nmanzil-pahuncho → kaam-karo(namak todo). \"Chalna, Pahunchna, Todna\" — teen alag verbs, teen alag dates.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDandi March START=12 March 1930. Dandi ARRIVAL=5 April 1930. CDM OFFICIALLY START(namak todkar)=6\nApril 1930 — teen alag dates, mix mat karo.\n4. 3 Round Table Conferences — Congress Ki Attendance\n●1st RTC(1930-31): Congress ABSENT\n●2nd RTC(1931): Gandhi(SOLE rep) · Churchill quote(\"half-naked Fakir\") ISI RTC mein\n●3rd RTC(1932): Congress BOYCOTTED\n●Ambedkar = SIRF EK VYAKTI jo TEENO RTC mein tha\n TRICK — \"Absent-Solo-Boycott\" progression trick\n💡\nCongress ka pattern: 1st=bilkul GAYAB(absent), 2nd=SIRF EK aadmi(Gandhi solo), 3rd=JAAN-BOOJHKAR","nahi gaye(boycott) — teen alag \"nahi-hone\" ke tareeke. Ambedkar hi EKLAUTA CONSTANT tha — teeno mein\npresent, is uniqueness ko yaad rakho.\nChurchill ka quote SIRF 2nd RTC ke context mein tha — jab Gandhi khud gaye the(kyunki tabhi Churchill ne unhe\ndekha/criticize kiya).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1st RTC=Congress Absent. 2nd RTC=Gandhi(sole rep) — Churchill's \"half-naked Fakir\" quote ISI RTC mein. 3rd\nRTC=Congress Boycotted. Ambedkar=teeno mein present, ekmatra vyakti.\n5. Communal Award(1932) → Poona Pact(1932)\n●Communal Award(16 Aug 1932,Ramsay MacDonald): Separate Electorate —\nMuslims+Sikhs+Christians+Europeans+Anglo-Indians AUR Harijans BHI(crucial addition)\n●Gandhi's fast(20 Sep 1932,Yerwada Jail) → Poona Pact(24 Sep 1932)\n●Signatories: Ambedkar(Depressed Classes) + Malaviya(Gandhi/Upper Caste) — Gandhi khud SIGN NAHI kiya\n●Result: Separate Electorate for Depressed Classes ABOLISH · Reserved seats 71→148\n TRICK — \"Harijan-crucial-add\" + \"Gandhi-nahi-signed\" trick\n💡\nCommunal Award mein Harijans ka add hona hi Gandhi ko FAST pe le gaya — baaki groups(Muslim,Sikh etc) se\nGandhi ko utna farq nahi pada, par HARIJAN wala part unhe UNACCEPTABLE laga.\nPoona Pact khud Gandhi ne SIGN NAHI kiya — Malaviya ne unki taraf se sign kiya(Ambedkar ne apni taraf se) —\nye ek IMPORTANT detail hai jo exam mein poochha jaata hai: \"Gandhi + Ambedkar\" bolna technically thoda galat hai,\nactual signers Malaviya+Ambedkar the.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPoona Pact ke actual SIGNATORIES = Ambedkar(Depressed Classes) + Malaviya(Gandhi ki taraf se) — Gandhi khud\nsign NAHI kiya. Communal Award mein Harijans bhi shamil the — yehi crucial addition thi jispe Gandhi fast pe gaye.\n6. 1937 Elections & Tripuri Crisis(1939)\n●Feb 1937 elections: Congress 8/11 provinces jeeti(Chief Minister tenure 28 mahine)\n●Haripura(1938): Bose UNOPPOSED president\n●Tripuri(1939): Bose ne Gandhi ke candidate Pattabhi Sitaramayya ko HARAYA → \"Sitaramayya's defeat is MY\ndefeat\"(Gandhi) → deadlock → Bose RESIGN → successor Rajendra Prasad\n●National Planning Committee(1938): Chairman NEHRU(Bose Congress President tha us waqt, par committee-head\nNehru)\n●Forward Bloc(3 May 1939) = Bose ne banaya\n TRICK — \"Bose jeeta par resign kiya\" + \"Nehru-not-Bose\" trick\n💡\nBose Tripuri mein JEETA, phir bhi RESIGN kiya(deadlock ki wajah se) — counter-intuitive: jeetne wala hi haar\nmaan gaya. \"Jeet ke bhi haar mani\" yaad rakho.\nNational Planning Committee = NEHRU-chairman, jabki BOSE us waqt Congress PRESIDENT tha — is\nmismatch(president ≠ committee-head) ko alag se yaad rakho, exam directly poochta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNational Planning Committee(1938) ka Chairman=Jawaharlal Nehru — Congress President us waqt Subhash Chandra\nBose tha, par committee-head Nehru the.\n7. Congress Socialist Party(1934) — President vs Secretary\n●President = Acharya Narendra Dev · General Secretary = Jayprakash Narayan(JP) · Founders: JP+Narendra\nDev+Lohia\n●Bihar Socialist Party(1931) = JP — ye CSP(1934) se PEHLE bani thi","TRICK — \"Dev=President, JP=Secretary\" trick\n💡\nNarendra Dev = President(N-D-P, teeno mein koi direct link nahi par bas ratt lo: Dev=top role). JP =\nSecretary(operational role) — dono roles yaad rakho, exam swap karke poochta hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCongress Socialist Party(1934): President=Acharya Narendra Dev. General Secretary=Jayprakash Narayan — role swap\nmat karo.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"SimonCommission(7-British,Birkenhead,JohnSimon) → MadrasSession1927(Ansari,not Nehru) →\nNehruReport1928(Motilal,not Jawaharlal)→Jinnah's14Points →\nLahoreSession1929(Nehru,PurnaSwaraj)→26Jan1930(1stIndependenceDay) → DandiMarch:\n12Mar(start)-5Apr(reach)-6Apr(CDM-officially) → 3RTCs: 1st-Absent,2nd-Gandhi(sole,Churchill-quote),3rd-\nBoycott,Ambedkar-all3 → GandhiIrwinPact(5Mar1931)→2ndRTC →\nCommunalAward(16Aug1932,+Harijans)→Gandhi-fast(20Sep)→PoonaPact(24Sep,Ambedkar+Malaviya-\nsigned,71→148) → GOIAct1935 → 1937elections(8/11)→Haripura1938(Bose-unopposed)→Tripuri1939(Bose beats\nPattabhi,resigns,RajendraPrasad-successor) → NationalPlanningCommittee=Nehru(not Bose) →\nForwardBloc(3May1939) → CSP1934(Dev-President,JP-Secretary)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye HIGHEST-WEIGHTAGE chapter hai poore Modern History mein.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) 3 RTCs: 1st=Absent, 2nd=Gandhi(sole,Churchill quote isi mein), 3rd=Boycott. Ambedkar=teeno mein.\n2) Poona Pact signatories=Ambedkar+Malaviya — Gandhi khud sign NAHI kiya.\n3) National Planning Committee(1938) Chairman=Nehru, jabki Congress President us waqt Bose tha.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Gandhian Era — Second Phase","TOWARDS INDEPENDENCE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 12 (Final Chapter, Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Pakistan Demand — 3 Alag Log, 3 Alag Stage\n●Idea(1930): Muhammad Iqbal(Allahabad Session) — alag nation ka suggestion\n●Naam \"Pakistan\"(1933): Choudhary Rahmat Ali ne rakha\n●Official Demand(23 Mar 1940,Lahore): Jinnah(Muslim League)\n TRICK — \"Idea-Naam-Demand\" 3-person trick\n💡\nIqbal(Idea,1930) → Rahmat Ali(Rakha naam,1933) → Jinnah(Jor se demand,1940) = \"I-R-J\" chronologically — teen\nalag log, teen alag role: soch(idea), naam(naming), aur formal maang(demand).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPakistan: Idea=Iqbal(1930). Naam=Rahmat Ali(1933). Official Demand=Jinnah(1940,Lahore) — teen alag log, ek\nsequence.\n2. Individual Satyagraha(1940) — Sequence Yaad Rakho\n●1st: Vinoba Bhave(17 Oct,Paunar Ashram) → 2nd: Jawaharlal Nehru → 3rd: Brahma Dutt(state exams mein\npoochha jaata hai)\n TRICK — \"V-N-B\" order trick\n💡\nVinoba → Nehru → Brahma Dutt = \"V-N-B\" — Vinoba SABSE PEHLE isliye kyunki wo Gandhi ke sabse\nvishwasi/spiritual follower the, phir bada naam(Nehru), phir teesra(Brahma Dutt, jo kam-famous hai isliye exam mein\nspecifically poochha jaata hai).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIndividual Satyagraha sequence: 1st=Vinoba Bhave, 2nd=Jawaharlal Nehru, 3rd=Brahma Dutt — 3rd wala specifically\nstate exams mein poocha jaata hai.\n3. Cripps Mission(1942) — \"Post-Dated Cheque\"\n●Head: Stafford Cripps(sent by Churchill) · Offer: Dominion Status + Constituent Assembly(after war)\n●Opt-out Clause = SABSE BADA TRAP(states alag ho sakti thi) · Gandhi: \"Post-dated cheque on a failing bank\"\n TRICK — \"Cheque jo kabhi cash nahi hoga\" trick\n💡\nPost-dated cheque = wo cheque jo ABHI kaam nahi aata, future date pe hi chalega — aur bank khud DUB rahi\nhai(failing) — matlab Gandhi keh rahe the ki promise TOH mila hai, par jab tak wo poora hoga, tab tak British power hi\nkhatam ho chuki hogi. Is metaphor ko poora samjho, ye exam mein quote-based hi poocha jaata hai.\n4. Quit India Movement(1942) — Jail + Jagah Ka Trap\n●Launch: 8 Aug 1942, Gowalia Tank Maidan(aaj = August Kranti Maidan), Mumbai\n●Gandhi ki jail = AGHA KHAN PALACE, Pune — Yerwada NAHI(wo 1930 CDM mein tha)\n●Aruna Asaf Ali = Tiranga fehraya · Usha Mehta = Congress Radio(14 Aug)\n TRICK — \"1942≠1930 jail\" trick\n💡\n2 alag movements, 2 alag jail: 1930 CDM → Yerwada Jail, 1942 Quit India → Agha Khan Palace — dono \"Gandhi\nki jail\" se related hain isliye confuse hota hai, par 12 SAAL ka gap aur alag jail. \"Naya movement(1942), Nayi\njail(Agha Khan)\".","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nQuit India Movement(1942) mein Gandhi ki jail = Agha Khan Palace(Pune). Yerwada Jail = 1930 CDM mein tha —\ndono alag movements, alag jail.\n5. Parallel Governments — 3 Alag \"Sabse\"\n●Balia(UP,Chittu Pandey) = SABSE PEHLI\n●Satara(Maharashtra,Nana Patil) = SABSE LAMBI(1946 tak)\n●Tamluk(Bengal) = Vidyut Vahini(Armed Electric Force) + cyclone relief\n TRICK — \"Balia-First, Satara-Longest, Tamluk-Unique\" trick\n💡\nTeen alag superlatives: Balia=TIME-first, Satara=DURATION-longest, Tamluk=WORK-unique(cyclone-\nrelief+apni khud ki force) — teen alag dimension mein \"sabse\", mix mat karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBalia = sabse pehli parallel govt. Satara = sabse lambi(1946 tak). Tamluk = Vidyut Vahini + cyclone relief ke liye\nunique — teen alag facts.\n6. INA — Founder vs Supreme Commander\n●Founder: Captain Mohan Singh(1942, idea Rash Bihari Bose ka bhi tha)\n●Supreme Commander: Bose(July 1943 se) · Provisional Govt(21 Oct 1943,Singapore)\n●Rani Jhansi Regiment(Mahila) = Lakshmi Sehgal\n TRICK — \"Mohan Singh shuru kiya, Bose sambhala\" trick\n💡\nMohan Singh = FOUNDER(shuru kiya,1942), Bose = LEADER(baad mein sambhala,1943) — same pattern jo\nbaar-baar dikhi hai(founder vs real-power) — is bar bhi \"pehle wala shuru karta hai, bada naam baad mein aata hai\"\npattern hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nINA Founder=Captain Mohan Singh(1942). Supreme Commander=Bose(July 1943 se) — dono alag roles, alag time.\n7. Red Fort Trial(1945) — 3 Dharm, 1 Lawyer\n●3 Accused: Dhillon(Sikh) + Sehgal(Hindu) + Shahnawaz(Muslim) — unity symbol\n●Main Lawyer: Bhulabhai Desai(Nehru bhi tha, par lead Desai ne kiya)\n TRICK — \"3 dharm ek saath\" trick\n💡\nTeen accused teen alag dharm se(Sikh-Hindu-Muslim) — INA ki unity ko symbolize karta hai, is TRIO ko yaad rakho.\nBhulabhai Desai = MAIN lawyer, Nehru sirf sahayak tha.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nRed Fort Trial(1945) main lawyer=Bhulabhai Desai(Nehru bhi tha par lead nahi kiya). 3 accused=Dhillon(Sikh)\n+Sehgal(Hindu)+Shahnawaz(Muslim).\n8. Cabinet Mission(1946) — \"LCA\" Code\n●Pethick Lawrence(Chairman) + Stafford Cripps + A.V.Alexander = \"LCA\"\n●Cripps DONO missions mein tha: 1942(Cripps Mission,head) + 1946(Cabinet Mission,member)\n●Pakistan alag NAHI accept ki — Loose Federation propose ki\n TRICK — \"Cripps = Double-Appearance\" trick\n💡","Cripps 2 baar aaya(1942 mein khud head tha, 1946 mein sirf ek member) — is REPEAT-appearance ko yaad rakho,\nexam \"Cripps kis mission mein tha\" ambiguously poochta hai — jawab: DONO.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nStafford Cripps DONO missions mein tha: Cripps Mission(1942, khud HEAD) aur Cabinet Mission(1946, sirf ek\nMEMBER \"LCA\" mein) — dono confuse mat karo.\n9. Interim Govt(1946) & Independence Act — Key Dates\n●Liaqat Ali Khan(ML) = FINANCE portfolio — powerful ministry ek ML member ko, unusual isliye common trap\n●Independence Act 3 dates: Introduced(4 Jul 1947) → Passed/Royal Assent(18 Jul 1947) → Effective(15 Aug 1947)\n TRICK — \"Liaqat-Finance\" + \"4-18-15\" trick\n💡\nLiaqat Ali Khan(ML) ko FINANCE mila — is \"unusual power to opposition\" ko yaad rakho, exam specifically ye\ntrap try karta hai.\n4→18→15: Introduce(4 Jul) → Pass(18 Jul,2 hafte baad) → Effective(15 Aug,ek mahine baad) — teen stage, teen alag\ndates, GAP se yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nLiaqat Ali Khan(Muslim League member) ko Interim Govt mein FINANCE portfolio mila — unusual/powerful\nassignment. Independence Act: Introduced(4Jul)→Passed(18Jul)→Effective(15Aug1947).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Pakistan: Iqbal(idea1930)-RahmatAli(naam1933)-Jinnah(demand1940) → IndividualSatyagraha: Vinoba-Nehru-\nBrahmaDutt → CrippsMission1942('post-dated cheque') →\nQuitIndia(8Aug1942,GowaliaTank=AugustKrantiMaidan,Gandhi-AghaKhanPalace) → ParallelGovts: Balia(first)-\nSatara(longest)-Tamluk(unique) → INA: MohanSingh(founder)-Bose(SupremeCommander,Jul1943) →\nRedFortTrial(Dhillon-Sehgal-Shahnawaz,BhulabhaiDesai-lawyer) → CabinetMission1946(LCA,Cripps-dono-missions)\n→ InterimGovt(LiaqatAli-Finance) → IndependenceAct: 4Jul(introduce)-18Jul(pass)-15Aug(effective)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye Modern History set ka LAST chapter hai!\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Gandhi ki jail 1942 mein=Agha Khan Palace, 1930 mein=Yerwada — do alag movements.\n2) INA Founder=Mohan Singh(1942). Supreme Commander=Bose(July1943) — do alag roles.\n3) Pakistan: Idea=Iqbal(1930), Naam=Rahmat Ali(1933), Demand=Jinnah(1940) — teen alag log.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Towards Independence (Final Chapter)","GOVERNOR, GOVERNOR-GENERAL & VICEROY — MEMORY\nTRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 13 (Final Chapter, Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Position Evolution — 3 Baar Naam Badla\n●Governor of Bengal(1757-1773, Plassey ke baad) → GG of Bengal(1773-1833, Regulating Act) → GG of India(1833-\n1858, Charter Act) → Viceroy(1858-1947, GOI Act)\n TRICK — \"G-G-G-V\" evolution trick\n💡\n4 stages: Governor(sirf Bengal,Company) → GG-Bengal(bada scope,Company) → GG-India(poora India,Company) →\nViceroy(Crown direct rule) — jitna aage jaao utna scope BADA hota gaya, aakhri stage mein Company khud khatam ho\ngayi(Crown ne le liya).\n2. GG of Bengal vs GG of India — Dono \"1st\"\n●Warren Hastings = 1st GG of BENGAL(1773, Regulating Act)\n●Lord William Bentinck = 1st GG of INDIA(1833, Charter Act)\n TRICK — \"Bengal-Hastings, India-Bentinck\" trick\n💡\nDono \"1st GG\" hain par ALAG SCOPE ke liye — Hastings = chota scope(Bengal) ka 1st, Bentinck = bada\nscope(poora India) ka 1st — sawaal mein \"Bengal\" ya \"India\" keyword dekho, wahi decide karega.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nWarren Hastings = 1st GG of BENGAL(1773). Lord William Bentinck = 1st GG of INDIA(1833) — dono \"pehle\" hain\npar alag positions ke liye.\n3. Canning — EK HI Vyakti, DO Titles\n●Lord Canning = Last Governor-General + FIRST Viceroy — EK HI PERSON, sirf position ka NAAM badla(GOI\nAct 1858 ke baad)\n TRICK — \"Naam badla, aadmi wahi\" trick\n💡\nCanning khud nahi badla, sirf USKA TITLE badla — 1857 Revolt ke baad jab Crown ne Company se power li, tabhi\n\"Governor-General\" \"Viceroy\" ban gaya, aur Canning us waqt jo bhi tha wahi \"pehla Viceroy\" ban gaya. Same pattern\njo Mughal(Babur-Akbar) mein tha, yahan \"same-person-do-title\" hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nLord Canning = Last Governor-General AUR First Viceroy — ek hi vyakti, sirf position ka naam GOI Act 1858 ke baad\nbadla.\n4. Awadh — Misgovernance, DOCTRINE OF LAPSE NAHI\n●Satara(1848,pehla)→Jhansi(1853)→Nagpur(1854) = sab Doctrine of Lapse se\n●Awadh(1856) = \"MISGOVERNANCE\"(kushasan) se liya gaya — Doctrine of Lapse se NAHI\n TRICK — \"Awadh = Odd One Out\" trick\n💡\nDalhousie ki saari annexations mein AWADH AKELA hai jo Doctrine of Lapse se NAHI aaya — baaki sab\nstates(Satara,Jhansi,Nagpur) is theory se liye gaye, Awadh alag reason(misgovernance) se — is \"odd one out\" ko\nhighlight karke yaad rakho, SABSE BADA TRAP hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠","Awadh(1856) = MISGOVERNANCE se liya gaya, Doctrine of Lapse se NAHI — baaki states(Satara,Jhansi,Nagpur)\nDoctrine of Lapse se the.\n5. Income Tax — James Wilson, Canning NAHI\n●Income Tax Canning ke TENURE mein laga, par LAGAYA James Wilson(1st Finance Member) ne\n TRICK — \"Tenure ≠ Levied by\" trick\n💡\nCanning ke RAAJ mein hua, par Canning ne KHUD nahi lagaya — jaise koi PM ke time koi law banti hai, par usko\nbanane wala Finance Minister hota hai, PM nahi. \"Kis ke time aur kisne kiya\" — do alag sawaal, do alag jawab.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIncome Tax Canning ke TENURE mein laga, par LEVY kiya James Wilson(1st Finance Member) ne — \"who levied\" ka\njawab Wilson hai, Canning nahi.\n6. \"Father of...\" Titles — 5 Alag Log\n●Cornwallis = Father of Civil Service(India)\n●Wellesley(\"Tiger of Bengal\") = Father of Subsidiary Alliance\n●Dalhousie = Father of Doctrine of Lapse\n●Ripon = Father of Local Self-Government\n●Metcalfe = Liberator of Press(1835) — \"Father\" nahi, \"Liberator\"\n TRICK — \"5 Fathers, 5 Systems\" trick\n💡\nCornwallis-CivilService, Wellesley-Subsidiary(Alliance), Dalhousie-Doctrine(Lapse), Ripon-LocalSelfGovt — 4\n\"Fathers\", pehle-letter se match karo: C-C, W-S(alag letter but yaad rakho \"Tiger\"), D-D, R-L. Metcalfe akela\n\"Liberator\" hai, \"Father\" nahi — is exception ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nCornwallis=Father of Civil Service. Wellesley=Father of Subsidiary Alliance. Dalhousie=Father of Doctrine of Lapse.\nRipon=Father of Local Self-Govt. Metcalfe=LIBERATOR of Press(not \"Father\").\n7. Curzon — SABSE ZYADA Commissions\n●Famine(1899-1900) · Irrigation(Colin Scott Moncrieff,1901) · Police(Andrew Fraser,1902→CID) ·\nUniversity(Thomas Raleigh,1902)\n●Bengal Partition(1905) = \"Sabse bada political blunder\" · Victoria Memorial = Architect William Emerson\n TRICK — \"4 Commissions\" trick\n💡\nCurzon = SABSE ZYADA commissions banane wala Viceroy(4: Famine,Irrigation,Police,University) — is\n\"commission-obsessed\" image se hi Curzon yaad rakho, aur uska AAKHRI/BADA GALTI(Bengal Partition) bhi isi\ntenure mein hui.\n8. Lord Linlithgow — Sabse Lamba Tenure(8 Saal)\n●1936-44(8 saal) = sabse lamba tenure wala Viceroy · Quit India Movement(1942) isi ke time\n●Cornwallis ka tomb = Ghazipur(UP) · MAO College(1875) = Lytton ke tenure mein(Sir Syed Ahmad Khan ne\nbanayi)\n TRICK — \"Linlithgow = Sabse Lamba\" trick\n💡\n8 saal = sabse LAMBA — is number ko yaad rakho, aur isi lambe tenure mein hi sabse BADA movement(Quit India)\nbhi hua, jaise lamba tenure = zyada bade events dekhne ka mauka.","9. Mountbatten — Last Viceroy + 1st GG Independent India\n●Mountbatten = Last Viceroy(pre-Independence) + 1st GG of INDEPENDENT India\n●Uske baad C. Rajagopalachari = 1st INDIAN GG\n TRICK — \"Mountbatten-Videshi-First, Rajaji-Desi-First\" trick\n💡\nMountbatten = 1st GG of independent India(par VIDESHI/British), Rajagopalachari = 1st INDIAN GG(desi) —\nsame pattern jaisa \"1st Female President(Besant,videshi) vs 1st Indian Female President(Naidu)\" tha(Ch.7) — videshi-\npehle, desi-baad mein pattern yahan bhi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMountbatten = 1st GG of Independent India(British). C. Rajagopalachari = 1st INDIAN(desi) GG — dono \"1st\" hain par\nalag category.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Evolution:\nGovernor(Clive)→GGBengal(WarrenHastings,1773)→GGIndia(Bentinck,1833)→Viceroy(Canning,1858,last-GG+1st-\nViceroy) → Cornwallis-CivilService,Wellesley-SubsidiaryAlliance(TigerOfBengal) → Bentinck-Sati(1829) →\nDalhousie-DoctrineOfLapse(Awadh=misgovernance-exception),Railway(1853) → IncomeTax=JamesWilson(Canning-\ntenure) → Lytton-VPA(1878)+MAOCollege(1875) → Ripon-LocalSelfGovt(1882) →\nCurzon-4Commissions+BengalPartition(1905) → HardingeII-CapitalShift+PartitionAnnul(1911) → Chelmsford-\nRowlatt+Jallianwala(1919) → Irwin-DandiMarch+GandhiIrwinPact(1931) → Linlithgow-Longest(8yrs)\n+QuitIndia(1942) → Wavell-CabinetMission(1946) → Mountbatten-\nLastViceroy+1stGG(1947)→Rajagopalachari-1stIndianGG\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye POORE Modern History series ka SABSE AAKHRI chapter hai!\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Warren Hastings=1st GG of BENGAL. Bentinck=1st GG of INDIA — alag scope.\n2) Awadh(1856)=Misgovernance se liya, Doctrine of Lapse se NAHI(baaki states iske through the).\n3) Income Tax Canning ke tenure mein laga, par LEVY kiya James Wilson ne.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.13 Governor, GG & Viceroy (Final Chapter)"];
